{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W7MZUGNUwBZNBjWQ2godft","type":"tool_result","content":"848\t| 19 | halt | `(lit 42)` | — | result | `42` | yes |\n849\t| 20 | **tail-effect halt** | run **outside the wrappers**, in two batches on one machine: a setup batch `(then (def! 's (stream/make 4)) (def! 'c (cursor-of s)))` run to halt (store writes persist across batches, as `lift_support.cljc:320-322` relies on), then the batch `(stream/next! c)` **marked `:tail? true` at the root**, `c` resolving through the store; no application precedes the call, so `K` is empty (any `let1` or wrapper would push a frame, §5.2 above) | append `\"B\"` | tail, `:next` | halts with `\"B\"` (4b: a tail effect with no frame to pop halts, `srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:205-211` stage 2; stack: the seam's empty-`K` case, §4.3), env free of `store-of` | yes |\n850\t| 21 | **free-env shadowing** (the review's row) | initial free env `{x 99}`; `(let1 f (fn [] x) ((fn [x] (f (next-of c))) 1))` | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next`; `E` at the read binds `x` to 1; root `free-env` carries `x 99` | the lowered `f` returns `99` (not nil, not 1) on every lane; **the one row the earlier design would have failed** | yes |\n851\t| 22 | nil-valued live register | `(let1 pair (fn [p q] (cat (cat [] p) q)) (pair nil (next-of c)))`: the `nil` operand is evaluated **before** the read and is live across it (`(cat nil (next-of c))` would give `(conj nil \"B\")`, the list `(\"B\")`, so a vector-building `pair` is used; there is no `vector` primitive, `vm.cljc:380-410`, and `pair` builds through the segment's `cat`) | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next`; `W` has a present key with `[:lit nil]` | `[nil \"B\"]` | yes |\n852\t| 23 | tail FFI bookkeeping | a `tail` parked record under a call id `P ∈ :ffi-call-ids` | — | parked, context `:parked`, bookkeeping clause of P4 | validator accepts; the **same valid tail under a key not in `:ffi-call-ids`** is `:parked-site` (P4); moving `site` to a non-tail call is `:site` (T1, which runs first) | **synthetic**: no primitive returns an FFI effect through a tail `:call` today (evaluator §1.6) |\n853\t| 24 | `act` FFI bookkeeping | 3's parked bookkeeping record under its call id | — | parked, P4 bookkeeping | validator accepts | 4b stage 2 |\n854\t\n855\tRefusal rows: `:yin.k/not-quiescent` (`a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-not-quiescent`,\n856\t`:591-603`); `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` (a register kernel stepped one\n857\tinstruction past a `:const`, asked to lift); `:yin.k/non-portable\n858\t:reason-mismatch` (the `:observe` hold, `:675-692`); and the validator's\n859\t**membership tampers**, each a row-set edit of a valid body before\n860\tlower: a window with an extra live key → `:window-extra`; a live key\n861\tremoved → `:window-missing`; `rd` added → `:window-self`; `rd` replaced\n862\tby another register → `:destination`; a return frame's `pc` moved after\n863\ta tail call → `:return-site`; a reason the site does not admit →\n864\t`:reason-mismatch`; a `:tail` row given a fourth slot → `:frame-shape`;\n865\tthe `[:lit nil]` of row 22 dropped → `:window-missing`; a `:reified`\n866\tact whose `pc−1` is not a capture → `:captured-site`; a parked act whose\n867\t`pc−1` is not `:park` → `:parked-site`; for E2, with row 21's initial\n868\tfree environment extended to `{x 99 y 7}`, the **unshadowed** free\n869\tbinding `y` in the act's `E` changed to `8` → `:free-env-mismatch`\n870\t(changing the lexical `x`, which is `1` at the read, trips nothing: E2\n871\tcompares off the lexical names), and the lexical `x` **removed** from\n872\t`E` → `:free-env-mismatch` (presence clause (a)); the root `free-env`\n873\trow given a reserved key → `:reserved-name` (X1). **A changed live value**\n874\t(e.g. `\"A\"` → `\"Z\"` in row 1's window) is not a membership defect and is\n875\tnot expected to be refused: it is tested by **execution parity** (the\n876\tlowered run's result differs from the reference), as the review ruled.\n877\t\n878\t### 5.3 Lanes\n879\t\n880\tThe `:semantic-register` lane's wait entries are canonical frames plus\n881\tengine fields. The de Bruijn lanes load `(:image (derive/stack-image v))`\n882\tand `(:image (derive/register-image v))` of `v = (:vector (project P))`\n883\tthrough `dvm/create-vm`/`rvm/create-vm`, run to the safepoint and lift\n884\tthrough `layout/lift-act`/`lift-tail`; the stack lane's tail rows (6,\n885\t9, 12, 20) require the seam of §4.3 and are gated on 6c-pre.\n886\t\n887\t### 5.4 Laws\n888\t\n889\t1. **Reference parity**: result and effect trace of the lowered,\n890\t   satisfied machine equal the reference run (`reference`/`handed-off`,\n891\t   `:368-401`).\n892\t2. **Round trip**: `lift(lower(S)) = S` by root id under the\n893\t   fresh-receiver context of the draft's §9, after the re-emission of\n894\t   §5.5.\n895\t3. **Observed reason**: the pending's reason is the wait's, never the\n896\t   static kind (ucf-revisions §8).\n897\t4. **Cross-engine canonical equality**: one program at one safepoint\n898\t   lifts to row sets whose root ids are **equal after the re-emission of\n899\t   §5.5** on all three lanes.\n900\t5. **Cross-engine lowering**: a row set lifted on one lane lowers on\n901\t   each of the other two (six ordered pairs) and continues to the\n902\t   reference result.\n903\t6. **Validator agreement**: every lifted frame passes `frame/defect` in\n904\t   its context; every tamper of §5.2 is refused with its kind; the\n905\t   verdict is lane-independent.\n906\t\n907\t### 5.5 Re-emission for equality (replacing \"stream-blinding\")\n908\t\n909\t**PROPOSED** (reviewer: `stream-blind` rewrites decoded maps and does\n910\tnot recompute Merkle ids, so it cannot establish root-id equality). The\n911\tharness first **fixes identities where it can**: all three lanes serve\n912\ttheir streams through one toy channel (`v2_support/toy`,\n913\t`served-peer`), so stream identities and descriptors are equal across\n914\tlanes by construction where the same logical stream is lifted. Where a\n915\tlane mints its own (fresh cursor cells on relift, the receiver's own call\n916\tpair), the comparison uses `rows/canonical-under`, a **test-only**\n917\ttransformation whose placeholder assignment is **never derived from\n918\t*host* traversal order** (the canonical walk of draft §6 is a function\n919\tof the state and is what the procedure reads; the review's objection: map and set traversal, and\n920\t\"cursor cells by body\", can depend on the very identities being erased). It\n921\ttakes an **explicit logical-stream correspondence** from the fixture:\n922\tthe harness created every stream the row reaches, so it supplies\n923\t`{lane-identity → logical-name}` (e.g. `{id-of-s :s, id-of-call-out\n924\t:call-out}`) for each lane; `canonical-under` decodes the row set to the\n925\tabstract task (draft §6's input), replaces each stream marker's identity\n926\tand descriptor by the logical name the map gives it (a marker the map\n927\tdoes not cover is a test failure, never a guess), runs the canonical\n928\tcursor-cell numbering (draft §6), re-emits every row and recomputes every id,\n929\tand compares root ids. Draft §6 is invariant under renaming of the\n930\t**cursor cells** (its labels never encode an incoming cursor-cell id), and the only\n931\tother identity it consumes is the stream marker in each cursor cell's body\n932\tlabel (`[:body [:stream identity descriptor] position]`, draft §6 as\n933\tamended, spelled by rank inside keys) and in cursor-cell bodies; after the substitution those are the fixture's\n934\tlogical names, so the procedure's inputs no longer depend on any lane's\n935\tidentities. Guest sets and maps are entered in the bytewise order of\n936\ttheir members' keys, and `:store`, `:bindings` and the parked table in\n937\tthe byte order of their structural keys (draft §6 W1), never in host\n938\tenumeration order, so\n939\ta permutation of the erased identities cannot change the result once\n940\tthe markers are substituted. It is never used outside the harness.\n941\t\n942\t### 5.6 Static checks the harness runs once per corpus segment\n943\t\n944\t1. `frame/defect` on every frame the reference lane mints: nil.\n945\t2. For every **reachable** parking pc `p` of `v`: `(analysis/saved a\n946\t   (inc p) rd)` has no member `≥ k(body(p))` and does not contain `rd`.\n947\t3. Register layout: at every reachable boundary pc `p`, `virt(p, s)` is\n948\t   single-valued on the physical image of `live-out*(p)`; the `live`\n949\t   operand of `R[p]` equals `(sort (map phys (disj live-out*(p) rd)))`,\n950\t   the destination removed as a **virtual** id before mapping, which is\n951\t   `[]` for a tail call (phase-5 §2.5). Worked example, inner call at\n952\t   `p = 3`: `L(4) = {1 2}`, minus `rd 2` → `{1}` → `[0]`, the pinned\n953\t   `live` of phase-5 §6.3 row 2.\n954\t4. Stack layout: the k-th non-push instruction of `H` has the mnemonic\n955\t   family of `v[k]` for every `k`; counts agree.\n956\t5. Stack layout: `(set (stack-layout p)) = (analysis/saved a (inc p)\n957\t   rd)` for every reachable **non-tail** parking pc `p`.\n958\t6. `E` reconstruction: at every safepoint reached, the layout's `E`\n959\t   equals the reference lane's `E` (values normalised), including rows\n960\t   21 and 22 and the `:duplicate-param`, `:nested-closure`,\n961\t   `:nested-lambdas` programs.\n962\t7. Closure reconstruction: canonical ↔ positional closures round-trip on\n963\t   the `\"closure value\"` and `\"higher order\"` B0 rows and\n964\t   `:duplicate-param`.\n965\t8. Tail lowering: the `:frames`/`:store-of` chosen for a lowered `tail`\n966\t   entry are unobservable: lowering with `[]`/`nil` and with arbitrary\n967\t   values gives equal observables on rows 6, 9, 12, 20.\n968\t9. Slices: for every non-tail safepoint with `m` return frames, the\n969\t   `m+1` slices of §4.3 partition the stack kernel's operand stack\n970\t   exactly, and each has the length of its `stack-layout`.\n971\t\n972\t---\n973\t\n974\t## 6. Code and task context in the carrier\n975\t\n976\t### 6.1 Code\n977\t\n978\t**DECIDED** (rulings 1, 3, 4; phase-5 §7.6, §9.2; v2 amendment §4's\n979\t2026-10-10 note). The root's `code` slot is plain `{A canonical-vector}`\n980\tof `\"v4\"` vectors, verified to hash to their key and to pass\n981\t`code/well-formed?`. **No native image travels**: a stack or register\n982\treceiver derives `H(A)`/`R(A)` with `derive/stack-image`/`register-image`.\n983\t`requires` carries UCF §7.6.1's map **plus** `:yin.k/trees {A #{tree-address …}}`,\n984\tone entry per address in `:yin.k/segments`; the **complete association\n985\trule** is phase-5's: an absent entry **or an empty set** is incomplete\n986\t(`:yin.k/missing :yin.k/trees`, discovery `:incomplete`), and a claimed\n987\taddress alone does not establish retrievability (a known address whose\n988\tread fails now is the medium's `:absent`, not a missing association).\n989\t\n990\t### 6.2 Rows, not datoms\n991\t\n992\t**DECIDED** (ruling 4). No vector is projected to datoms; the direct\n993\tload path is the only path (§10.4).\n994\t\n995\t### 6.3 The free environment: carrier, source, ownership\n996\t\n997\t**DECIDED** by the review's finding and §4.4. The task's initial free\n998\tenvironment travels **once, explicitly**, as the root's `free-env`\n999\tslot, a `:bindings` row (`[S V …]` sorted). Every `E` in the task is a\n1000\tcomplete map and is checked by rules X1 and E2. On lower, the\n1001\tsemantic-register kernel receives it as the machine's base `:env`\n1002\t(`create-vm`'s `:env` option, `semantic_register.cljc:261`); a de Bruijn\n1003\tkernel receives it as its `:free-env` (`stack.cljc:418`) and\n1004\treconstructs positional frames from each `E` by the chain (§4.4).\n1005\t\n1006\t**Where the lift gets it (PROPOSED, the gap the review named).** It is\n1007\t**never recovered from a current `E`** (§4.4). Its source is, per\n1008\tkernel:\n1009\t\n1010\t- **de Bruijn kernels**: the kernel's own `:free-env` field, \"fixed for\n1011\t  this instance\" (`stack.cljc:82`; `register.cljc:50`), read directly.\n1012\t- **the semantic-register kernel**: the evaluator keeps only the\n1013\t  mutable-current `:env` (`RegisterVM` field `env`, \"persistent lexical\n1014\t  scope map\", `srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:23`; the old semantic\n1015\t  VM likewise captures the initial env only transiently in `eval`,\n1016\t  `semantic.cljc:874-876`), so no field holds the initial map. The\n1017\t  **composition owns it**: it is the value the composition passed as\n1018\t  `create-vm`'s `:env` (`vm/check-bindings!` of it, `:261`). The lift's\n1019\t  input contract therefore takes it explicitly,\n1020\t  `(rows/lift-task vm serve! {:free-env E₀})`, and refuses\n1021\t  `:yin.k/non-portable :missing-free-env` when the caller supplies none;\n1022\t  the holder and REPL paths that call the lift pass the environment they\n1023\t  constructed the task with. **Coordinated retention seam, recommended**:\n1024\t  4b (stage 3, its track's file) adds an immutable `free-env` field set\n1025\t  once in `create-vm` from the checked `:env` and never written by any\n1026\t  transition, with `gc-roots` listing it; once it lands the lift reads\n1027\t  it when `:free-env` is not supplied and the explicit argument stays as\n1028\t  the override for compositions that constructed the task elsewhere.\n1029\t  Phase 6 does **not** edit `semantic_register.cljc`; 6b depends on the\n1030\t  explicit argument and names the seam as a follow-up (§8.2).\n1031\t\n1032\tMerkle sharing means every `E` whose bindings equal another's shares one\n1033\t`:bindings` row; the root slot is one more reference to a row that\n1034\tusually already exists.\n1035\t\n1036\t---\n1037\t\n1038\t## 7. Lift and lower\n1039\t\n1040\t### 7.1 Lift\n1041\t\n1042\t**DECIDED** (draft §9, UCF §7.8): refuse unless quiescent; refuse the\n1043\tholds (`unliftable-hold`, `handoff.cljc:588`) as `:yin.k/non-portable\n1044\t:reason-mismatch`; classify kind; run the **dependency closure over the\n1045\t`\"v4\"` vectors**, which needs the phase-5 scanners\n1046\t(`scan/requirements`, `scan/free-names`, `scan/free-occurrences` over the\n1047\t§2.3 table: the current `completion/code-facts` reads stack-table\n1048\tpositions and cannot be used), and refuse `:yin.k/unsatisfied` unless\n1049\t`:complete`, `:yin.k/trees` included; number cursor cells (draft §6); walk\n1050\twaits, parked records, the store slice, module stores, the free\n1051\tenvironment (from the kernel's `:free-env` field or the lift's explicit\n1052\t`:free-env` argument, §6.3, never from a current `E`), the result,\n1053\tinstall children; run `frame/defect` over every\n1054\tframe; emit rows and the census. A de Bruijn source walks the frames\n1055\t`layout/lift-act`/`lift-tail` reconstruct.\n1056\t\n1057\t### 7.2 Lower\n1058\t\n1059\t**DECIDED** (draft §8 in order; §3.3): gate, structure, graph, hashes,\n1060\tcanonical form, canonical numbering, **frames**, pending and operations,\n1061\tdependency closure (`requires`/`code` agree with the census;\n1062\t`:yin.k/trees` complete per §6.1), custody, composition, restore. Restore\n1063\tbuilds the receiving kernel's state: semantic-register: `code` through\n1064\t`load-vector`/`attach-image` under `code/contract`, the free environment\n1065\tas base `:env`, each `:wait` to an engine entry (payload plus the\n1066\tpending's engine fields, `lower-frame!`'s shapes, `handoff.cljc:3182-3246`,\n1067\t`:deliver` carried), parked records into `:parked`, the result into\n1068\t`:value`; de Bruijn: derive and attach the image for each A, set\n1069\t`:free-env`, and `layout/lower-act`/`lower-tail` each frame (the stack\n1070\tlane's `tail` needs 6c-pre). Restoration delivers nothing, runs nothing,\n1071\tmints nothing.\n1072\t\n1073\t---\n1074\t\n1075\t## 8. Slices, gates, entry conditions\n1076\t\n1077\tVerification follows `docs/agents/build-n-test.md`: G0 per iteration on\n1078\tthe JVM, G1 `bb test:sub yin.vm` on three hosts, G2 `bb test:changed`,\n1079\tG3 on master.\n1080\t\n1081\t### 8.1 Slice 6a: the frame validator and the row codec (independent)\n1082\t\n1083\t**Files to create.**\n1084\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc` (§3): `defect`, public.\n1085\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` (§2): the row table as data,\n1086\t  `frame->rows`, `rows->frame`, row ids (Jing default), the census and\n1087\t  numbering per the draft §6, `canonical-under` (§5.5, test-only but\n1088\t  placed here so three test namespaces share it). **Not** `lift-task`/\n1089\t  `lower-task`: full task transport is 6b.\n1090\t- `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame_test.cljc`,\n1091\t  `test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc`.\n1092\t\n1093\t**Depends on:** phase 3, 4a (landed), 4b stage 1 (branch) for live\n1094\tframes to validate. Touches nothing of 4b or 5; needs no scanner.\n1095\t\n1096\t**Acceptance (6a).**\n1097\t\n1098\t1. `frame-test/contract-is-pure`: `frame/defect` takes `[frame code\n1099\t   context task]`, `task` being plain data; the namespace's `ns` form\n1100\t   requires no kernel and no `yin.vm.engine` (a string check over the\n1101\t   source on the JVM lane, `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)`).\n1102\t2. `frame-test/every-reference-frame-validates`: for every 4b-stage-1\n1103\t   row of §5.2 (1, 2, 5, 6, 13-16, 18, 19, 21, 22) over the four segments,\n1104\t   plus row 20 as one separate, unwrapped run (its empty `K` needs no wrapper\n1105\t   frames; §8.2 6b makes the same exception), every\n1106\t   `act`, `tail`, return frame, parked record and reified value the\n1107\t   register evaluator mints passes `defect` in its context with the\n1108\t   task context decoded from the machine's own tables.\n1109\t3. `frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper`: for each rule S1-S4, C1-C3,\n1110\t   A1-A6, T1, K1-K3, E1-E2, X1, P1-P4 one tampered frame built from a\n1111\t   valid one, refused with that rule's kind and a path naming the slot\n1112\t   (**twenty-four rules**: 4+3+6+1+3+2+1+4, the twenty-three of the\n1113\t   round-1 text plus X1; **twenty-five rows**, since C2 contributes two,\n1114\t   a float `pc` for `:pc-kind` and an out-of-range one for `:pc-bounds`;\n1115\t   X1's row goes through `frame/task-defect`); plus\n1116\t   `first-defect-is-structural`: a frame with a malformed `K` **and** a\n1117\t   bad window reports `:k-shape`.\n1118\t4. `frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member`: row 22's frame\n1119\t   validates with the nil key present; the same frame with the key\n1120\t   removed is `:window-missing`.\n1121\t5. `frame-test/worked-example-saved`: on `:worked-example`, a frame at pc\n1122\t   4 with window `{1 <f>}` and `rd 2` validates; `{1 <f> 2 x}` is\n1123\t   `:window-self`; `{}` is `:window-missing`; `{1 <f> 3 x}` is\n1124\t   `:window-extra` (`saved(4, 2) = {1}`, `analysis_test.cljc:131-139`).\n1125\t6. `frame-test/free-env-mismatch`: row 21's frame (initial free\n1126\t   environment `{x 99 y 7}`) with `task :free-env {x 99 y 7}` validates;\n1127\t   with the free environment `{x 99 y 8}` or `{x 99}` it is\n1128\t   `:free-env-mismatch` (`y` is unshadowed); with the lexical `x` removed\n1129\t   from `E` it is `:free-env-mismatch` (presence); changing the lexical\n1130\t   `x` in `E` from `1` to `98` **does not** trip E2 (it is off the\n1131\t   comparison), and the test asserts that too; a `free-env` row with the\n1132\t   key `yin/def` is `:reserved-name` (X1).\n1133\t7. `rows-test/bijection`: `frame->rows ∘ rows->frame` and the converse\n1134\t   are identities on every frame of item 2, nil-valued keys included.\n1135\t8. `rows-test/row-ids-are-jing-default`: every content row's id equals\n1136\t   `(jing/segment-key body)` and names Jing's default algorithm; no\n1137\t   `sha256` appears in any id.\n1138\t9. `rows-test/window-sorted-and-unique`: an out-of-order or duplicated\n1139\t   `:window` row is `:yin.k/undecodable` at canonical form (step 5).\n1140\t10. `rows-test/canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`: §5.5's\n1141\t    transformation gives equal root ids for two emissions of one abstract\n1142\t    task under permuted cursor-cell numbering and distinct stream identities,\n1143\t    with the fixture's correspondence map; **and the unordered-container\n1144\t    permutation**: a store value that is a set of two stream references\n1145\t    and a map keyed by two cursor references, emitted twice with the two\n1146\t    streams' identities swapped (and the correspondence map swapped\n1147\t    accordingly), gives equal root ids; a marker absent from the map is\n1148\t    a test failure.\n1149\t11. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts; Node log\n1150\t    shows `Testing yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test` and\n1151\t    `Testing yin.vm.ucf.rows-test`.\n1152\t12. `rows-test/discovery-order-numbering`: `canonical-numbering` returns\n1153\t    the maps of the numbering note's appendix A for `fixture :s1 :s2 :x\n1154\t    :y`, the review counterexample, `[x x y]`, `[x y y]`, `[#{X Y} X]`,\n1155\t    the witness `[#{#{[A B] [B A]}} A]`, `[#{X Y} #{Y Z}]`, the path and\n1156\t    the two frame fixtures.\n1157\t13. `rows-test/occurrence-count-separates-members`: the review\n1158\t    counterexample numbers `Y cc-1, X cc-2`, pinned `2d9873a8…`; the path\n1159\t    pinned `726a9fbb…`; `[#{X Y} #{Y Z}]` pinned `d84480d4…`; each equal\n1160\t    after renaming plus reversal of every set.\n1161\t14. `rows-test/interchangeable-ties`: `#{X Y}`, `#{[X X] [Y Y]}`,\n1162\t    `{X 1, Y 1}`, `#{#{X Y} #{Z W}}` number without refusal; reversal and\n1163\t    renaming give equal roots; pins `07eda35d…`, `da69c679…`,\n1164\t    `49d4478c…`, `18b70de6…`.\n1165\t15. `rows-test/alias-pattern-is-part-of-the-key`: `#{[X X] [Y Z]}` and\n1166\t    `{X X, Y Z}` give one root for both enumerations and after renaming,\n1167\t    pinned `387f294a…` and `be62ba43…`; the witness numbers `B cc-1,\n1168\t    A cc-2`, pinned `0193312…`, and decodes; the balanced-alias witness\n1169\t    `#{[X X Y Y] [Z W Z W]}` gives one root for both enumerations, pinned\n1170\t    `5376f133…`, and the key without the local index would not.\n1171\t16. `rows-test/unresolved-cursor-cells-refuse`: the 2-cycle, the\n1172\t    3-cycle, the loop plus 2-cycle, the seven-cell state,\n1173\t    `[#{X Y} #{X Y}]`, the mixed-body, the anchored, the two-2-cycle and\n1174\t    the 3-cycle-beside-fan states refuse at `emit` with\n1175\t    `:yin.k/non-portable :unresolved-cursor-cells`, the paths and cells of\n1176\t    the numbering note's appendix A, the same verdict and path after\n1177\t    renaming plus shuffling; a carrier of each built with `emit-numbered`\n1178\t    decodes to `:yin.k/undecodable :unresolved-cursor-cells` with the\n1179\t    path prefixed by the root, never `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`; a\n1180\t    parent whose install `'a` holds the 2-cycle refuses at `emit` with\n1181\t    path `[12 a 15]` and its `emit-numbered` carrier decodes to the\n1182\t    `:yin.k/undecodable` kind with path `[<root> 12 a 15]`.\n1183\t17. `rows-test/canonical-roots-are-pinned`: `fab223…` and `c4a7c7…`\n1184\t    unchanged; `a850fce6…` (`[#{X Y} X]`), `4993b5b1…`, `536c810b…`,\n1185\t    `e67405ec…` (`[#{#{X Y} #{Z W}} X]`), `6e7c7a6b…` (ten cells) added;\n1186\t    `55ff168e…` removed.\n1187\t18. `rows-test/counterexample-search`: a seeded generator (at least 2000\n1188\t    random value states, 200 frame-bearing, 100 with install children)\n1189\t    in CI: every numbered state's carrier decodes and re-emits to its\n1190\t    root; renaming every cursor cell plus shuffling every set, map and\n1191\t    census gives an equal root, or the same refusal verdict and path;\n1192\t    refusals are counted and reported; the largest `:work` is reported.\n1193\t19. `rows-test/numbering-is-total`: a census cell the walk does not reach\n1194\t    raises the totality defect, not a refusal, before any row is emitted.\n1195\t20. `numbering-precedes-frame-defect`, `alias-topology-and-census`,\n1196\t    `canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`,\n1197\t    `unordered-containers-are-order-free`,\n1198\t    `child-scope-and-shared-child-dag` and\n1199\t    `census-is-numeric-from-ten-cursor-cells` pass unchanged against the\n1200\t    rewritten decoder; `numbering-precedes-frame-defect` is extended: the\n1201\t    2-cycle with the same reserved-name binding, carried by\n1202\t    `emit-numbered`, decodes to `:yin.k/undecodable\n1203\t    :unresolved-cursor-cells`, not `:reserved-name`.\n1204\t21. `rows-test/gates-and-work`: 65 cells refuse `:resource-limit\n1205\t    [:cursor-cells]` under the default budget and 2 cells under\n1206\t    `{:cursor-cells 1}`; `[[[[X]]]]` under `{:depth 3}` refuses\n1207\t    `[:depth]`, and so do one cell inside 3000 nested vectors under\n1208\t    `{:depth 3}` and under the default budget, and a literal nested 3000\n1209\t    deep beside a cell (no host stack overflow on any of the three hosts;\n1210\t    200 nested vectors number); a set holding a 400000-scalar literal\n1211\t    refuses `[:work]` under `{:work 2000}` with the work counter at 2001\n1212\t    and under `{:work 900000}` with at most 1000 estimator steps; a state\n1213\t    whose bodies carry a 65536-character descriptor numbers under the\n1214\t    default budget; `{:work 1}` refuses `[:work]` at `emit` and, for a\n1215\t    valid carrier, at `decode`.\n1216\t22. Budgets: `:label-bytes` and `:search` gone, `:work` default\n1217\t    `4194304`.\n1218\t\n1219\t### 8.2 Slice 6b: full task transport and the harness on the reference lane\n1220\t\n1221\t**Files to change.** `rows.cljc`: `lift-task`, `lower-task` (§7), the\n1222\tpending rows' lift and lower, install children. **Files to create.**\n1223\t`test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc` (§5, the\n1224\t`:semantic-register` lane). The old harness file is not edited.\n1225\t\n1226\t**Depends on:** the explicit `:free-env` lift argument supplied by the\n1227\tharness (§6.3; the 4b retention seam is a named follow-up for the 4b\n1228\ttrack, not a 6b prerequisite); 4b stage 2 (FFI retained→sent restoration, link\n1229\trequest/response/install preservation, install children, the\n1230\tevaluator's `IModuleKernel` linking methods: `link-format`,\n1231\t`spawn-module`, `lift-closure`, `lower-closure`); **phase 5c** (the\n1232\t`scan` namespace, for the dependency closure over `\"v4\"` vectors, §7.1).\n1233\tTouches nothing of 4b or 5.\n1234\t\n1235\t**Acceptance (6b).**\n1236\t\n1237\t1. `every-row-every-segment-matches-the-reference`: rows 1-19, 21, 22\n1238\t   and 24 of §5.2 × four segments, plus row 20 once (outside the\n1239\t   wrappers, §5.2), on the reference lane; laws 1-3 and 6; counts\n1240\t   asserted (22 wrapped rows × 4 segments + 1 = 89 runs).\n1241\t2. `tail-states-carry-no-window`: rows 6, 9, 12, 20 lift to `:tail`\n1242\t   rows of three slots and lower to through-`K` delivery.\n1243\t3. `install-rows-carry-the-child`: rows 10-12; the child's kind and\n1244\t   phase as stated; no initialization on lower.\n1245\t4. `captures`: rows 14-16 round-trip; row 15's invocation after lower\n1246\t   delivers once into the captured `rd` and yields `:done`.\n1247\t5. `free-env-shadowing`: row 21 yields `99` after lower.\n1248\t6. `synthetic-tail-bookkeeping`: row 23's hand-built parked `tail`\n1249\t   under a call id in `:ffi-call-ids` passes `defect` with context\n1250\t   `:parked`; the **same valid record under a key absent from\n1251\t   `:ffi-call-ids`** is `:parked-site` (P4); the record with `site` moved\n1252\t   to a non-tail call is `:site` (T1 runs before P4).\n1253\t7. `refusals`: every refusal row of §5.2 refuses with the named status\n1254\t   and kind before any attachment; `first-defect-order`: a body with a\n1255\t   noncanonical cursor-cell numbering **and** a tampered window reports\n1256\t   `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`.\n1257\t8. `a-response-cursor-shared-by-two-waiters-crosses-as-one-cursor-cell` and\n1258\t   `a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-not-quiescent`, ported.\n1259\t9. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts.\n1260\t\n1261\t### 8.3 Slice 6c: the layouts, the stack seam, the cross-engine lanes\n1262\t\n1263\t**6c-pre, the stack tail-completion seam.** File to change:\n1264\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc` (§4.3): park-entry builders mark a\n1265\ttail-call park `:resume-mode :return-result`; `stack-restore` delivers\n1266\tsuch an entry by the return transition. Test to create:\n1267\t`test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_tail_completion_test.cljc`: a tail\n1268\teffectful call parked and resumed delivers through `K` (pops the frame,\n1269\ttruncates to its base, pushes the value) and halts with the value when\n1270\t`K` is empty; a tail call in operand position never executes the layout\n1271\tsyntax after it; non-tail parks are unchanged (the old stack tests stay\n1272\tgreen). **Depends on** nothing of 4b or 5.\n1273\t\n1274\t**6c proper.** Files to create: `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc`\n1275\t(§4); `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc`; the two extra\n1276\tlanes added to the 6b harness file. **Depends on:** 5a, 5b (`derive`),\n1277\t6b, 6c-pre.\n1278\t\n1279\t**Acceptance (6c).**\n1280\t\n1281\t1. `layout-test/register-pairing`: for every `P ∈ C`, `phys` is total on\n1282\t   every body's named virtuals; `virt(p, s)` is single-valued at every\n1283\t   reachable boundary pc (§5.6 item 3).\n1284\t2. `layout-test/register-live-is-live-out`: §5.6 item 3's second clause,\n1285\t   tail boundaries `[]`.\n1286\t3. `layout-test/register-rd-from-a`: on `:worked-example`'s register\n1287\t   lane at the inner call's park, the canonical `rd` is `2` while the\n1288\t   kernel's `dest` is `3`; the K frame of a nested non-tail call in\n1289\t   `:depth-3` has its `rd` from A, not its physical `dest`.\n1290\t4. `layout-test/stack-correspondence`: §5.6 item 4.\n1291\t5. `layout-test/stack-layout-is-the-saved-set`: §5.6 item 5 and the\n1292\t   worked cases: `(f (g x) y)` at the inner call → `[1]`; `(f (if c (g)\n1293\t   2) y)` at `(g)` → `[1]`.\n1294\t6. `layout-test/stack-slices-partition`: §5.6 item 9; and the\n1295\t   multi-frame fixture, the expression `(cat [1] ((fn [x] (cat [2] ((fn\n1296\t   [y] (cat [3] (next-of c))) 2))) 1))` under the harness's standard\n1297\t   binding setup: `with-cat` outermost, then `(let1 s (stream/make 4)\n1298\t   (let1 c (cursor-of s) …))` around it (the stream is made inside the\n1299\t   program, as every row does: that is this fixture's chosen setup. A\n1300\t   primitive `cat` supplied in the free environment would sit in a live\n1301\t   slot and is no carrier value, `:continuation-registers`,\n1302\t   `debruijn_register_effects.cljc:196`; an authentic cursor reference is\n1303\t   machine data with an explicit carrier marker, `engine.cljc:899-905`, so\n1304\t   in-program construction of `c` is a fixture choice, not a carrier\n1305\t   restriction). **Derivation of the expression\n1306\t   alone** (`cat` and `c` taken as given): the outer application of\n1307\t   `(fn [x] …)` pops its closure and `1`, leaving the outer `cat` and\n1308\t   `[1]` pushed, so its frame's base is `2`; the inner application leaves\n1309\t   the middle `cat` and `[2]` as well, base `4`; the current activation\n1310\t   has pushed its `cat` and `[3]` and the read has popped its cursor\n1311\t   operand (`stack.cljc:839`), so the operand stack has six values:\n1312\t   slices `[0,2)` = `[cat [1]]`, `[2,4)` = `[cat [2]]`, current `[4,6)` =\n1313\t   `[cat [3]]`, each slice's `stack-layout` being `[operator-rd\n1314\t   literal-rd]` of its `cat` call and equal to that activation's saved\n1315\t   window. **As run**, the three binding applications each pop their\n1316\t   closure and single operand off an otherwise empty stack, so `K` has\n1317\t   **five** frames with bases `0, 0, 0, 2, 4`, slices `[0,0) [0,0) [0,0)\n1318\t   [0,2) [2,4)`, current `[4,6)`, stack length six; the test pins these\n1319\t   bases from the kernel's state, checks the partition, and checks that\n1320\t   lowering the lifted frame emits the same five bases (§4.3; the\n1321\t   before-slice rule would emit `0, 0, 0, 0, 2`).\n1322\t7. `layout-test/env-reconstruction`: §5.6 item 6.\n1323\t8. `layout-test/closures-round-trip`: §5.6 item 7.\n1324\t9. `layout-test/tail-lowering-is-unobservable`: §5.6 item 8.\n1325\t10. `harness/cross-engine-canonical-equality`: law 4 for every row ×\n1326\t    segment under `canonical-under`.\n1327\t11. `harness/cross-engine-lowering`: law 5, six ordered pairs.\n1328\t12. `harness/layout-refusals`: `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` from a kernel\n1329\t    stepped to a non-safepoint pc; a register entry whose `live` was\n1330\t    tampered reconstructs a frame the validator refuses (`:window-extra`\n1331\t    or `:window-missing` by the tamper's direction).\n1332\t13. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts.\n1333\t\n1334\t### 8.4 Phase 7's entry conditions\n1335\t\n1336\t**DECIDED** (frozen §10 phase 7). 6a-6c green on three hosts; the row\n1337\tcarrier the only writer and reader the semantic-register kernel has; a\n1338\tdocumented seam for the holder, checkpoint, ledger and authority paths\n1339\t(phase 7 wires it; phase 6 edits none of them); the Stage D/E scenarios\n1340\t(`stage_e_scenarios.cljc`, `checkpoint_fixtures.cljc`) listed with, for\n1341\teach, the §5.2 row that exercises its parking shape; the export-recovery\n1342\tobject (UCF §7.7.4, format version 1 over the old codec) re-based on the\n1343\trow carrier by phase 7, since it embeds a body; and the free-environment\n1344\tretention seam (§6.3) either landed by the 4b track or the explicit\n1345\t`:free-env` argument threaded through the holder's export path.\n1346\t\n1347\t### 8.5 Ordering and concurrency\n1348\t\n1349\t| | needs | concurrent with |\n1350\t|---|---|---|\n1351\t| 6a | 4b stage 1 (branch) | 4b stage 2, 5a-5c, 6c-pre |\n1352\t| 6c-pre | nothing of 4b or 5 | everything |\n1353\t| 6b | 4b stage 2; 5c (scanners) | 5a, 5b, 6c-pre |\n1354\t| 6c | 5a, 5b, 6b, 6c-pre | 5c |\n1355\t\n1356\tNo file of 4b or phase 5 is edited. The old kernel file\n1357\t`debruijn/stack.cljc` is edited by 6c-pre only, for the seam; the\n1358\tregister kernel is not edited. `handoff.cljc` and the old harness are\n1359\tnot edited.\n1360\t\n1361\t---\n1362\t\n1363\t## 9. Verification honesty\n1364\t\n1365\t- **Hand-derived numbers.** `saved(4, 2) = {1}` and `L(5)` on the worked\n1366\t  example are the phase-3 tests' (`analysis_test.cljc:131-139`). The\n1367\t  stack slices `[f]` at the inner call of `(f (g x) y)` and at `(g)` in\n1368\t  `(f (if c (g) 2) y)` were derived twice from the §4.3 walk and agreed\n1369\t  with the reviewer's derivation; the register `phys(1) = 0`, `phys(2) =\n1370\t  3` follow from phase-5 §6.3 row 2, whose pinned `live` at pc 3 is `[0]`\n1371\t  (`{T0,T3}` minus the destination `T3`), the same set §4.2 step 4 and\n1372\t  §5.6 item 3 compute by subtracting the virtual `rd 2` before mapping.\n1373\t  The multi-frame bases in 6c item 6 (`2, 4` for the expression alone;\n1374\t  `0, 0, 0, 2, 4` as run under the harness's bindings) were derived\n1375\t  twice from the kernel's call arm (`stack.cljc:716-733`, base = height\n1376\t  after popping callee and operands); the first pass forgot the pushed\n1377\t  operator, and revision 2's lowering rule used the height **before**\n1378\t  each slice, which the round-2 review caught and §4.3 now states as\n1379\t  cumulative through the slice. Nothing was run.\n1380\t- **Claims that are checks, not theorems**: the stack operand slice\n1381\t  equals the saved set at non-tail safepoints (§5.6 item 5); the non-push\n1382\t  H ↔ A correspondence (item 4); `virt` single-valued at reachable\n1383\t  boundaries (item 3); layout `E` = evaluator `E` (item 6); the tail\n1384\t  lowering's unused fields are unobservable (item 8); the slices\n1385\t  partition the stack (item 9).\n1386\t- **What is not claimed**: that kernel state round-trips (shadowed outer\n1387\t  positional values are nil-filled; the law is on canonical frames);\n1388\t  that every kernel reconstructs canonical frames (two are named; the\n1389\t  walker is excluded); that today's stack kernel delivers a tail effect\n1390\t  through `K` (it does not; 6c-pre adds it).\n1391\t- **Private access.** Every function a test names is public; no `#'`.\n1392\t- **Unverified.** 4b stage 2 is not landed: rows 3-4, 7-12, 17, 24 are\n1393\t  written against the evaluator design's §1.4-1.6 shapes and the stage-1\n1394\t  branch and must be re-read when stage 2 lands. The seam of §4.3 is a\n1395\t  specification of a change to `stack.cljc`, not a reading of code that\n1396\t  exists.\n1397\t\n1398\t---\n1399\t\n1400\t## 10. Findings and proposed amendments\n1401\t\n1402\tReviewer rulings (codex gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-10-10): F1, F4, U2, U4, U5,\n1403\tR1, R2, R7, C1 **ACCEPT**; F2, F3, U1, U3, U6, R3, R4, R5, R6, R8, R9\n1404\t**ACCEPT WITH CHANGES**, applied below; dropping `:yin.k/engine`\n1405\t**ACCEPTED**; the merged-`E` free environment **REJECTED**, replaced by\n1406\t§4.4/§6.3.\n1407\t\n1408\t### 10.1 To the frozen design (`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`)\n1409\t\n1410\t**F1 — §4.2 row names (ACCEPT).** Replace \"`:regs` becomes `[segment-A\n1411\tpc env-cref window-cref k-cref deliver-D]` for an `act` and a sibling\n1412\t`:tail-state [segment-A site k-cref deliver-D]` is added\" with: \"the\n1413\tframe rows are `:act [segment-A pc env-cref window-cref k-cref rd]` and\n1414\t`:tail [segment-A site k-cref]`, the kind being the delivery\n1415\tdiscriminant, so `deliver` is not a slot; `:window` is a keyed row\n1416\t`[r₁ V₁ r₂ V₂ …]` sorted by `r` in which a nil-valued register is a\n1417\tpresent `[:lit nil]`; `:kframe` is `[segment-A pc env-cref window-cref\n1418\trd]`; `:stack` and `stack-base` are removed; the root gains `free-env`,\n1419\tthe task's initial free environment (continuation design §2, §6.3).\"\n1420\t\n1421\t**F2 — §4.2 the validator (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** After \"and pending\n1422\tcompatibility with `reason`\" insert: \"The validator is the pure function\n1423\t`(defect frame code context task)` of `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md`\n1424\t§3: `task` is decoded task context (the parked key, the live FFI call\n1425\tids, the free environment), never an engine; its rules are ordered,\n1426\tstructural checks first, current-window rules on `act` only, return\n1427\twindows separately, and every `E` is checked to agree with the task's\n1428\tfree environment off the lexical names; it runs after canonical\n1429\tnumbering, as the carrier orders it.\"\n1430\t\n1431\t**F3 — §4.3 foreign engines (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** After\n1432\t\"`lift(lower(frame)) = frame` holds for admitted canonical frames, as\n1433\ttoday.\" insert: \"The register kernel pairs physical and virtual\n1434\tregisters pc by pc from `v` and `R(v)`, recovers every destination from\n1435\tA's call (its `dest` is physical), and resolves each return frame's\n1436\timage and relative pc independently; the stack kernel corresponds the\n1437\tnon-push instructions of `H(v)` with `v`, slices its operand stack\n1438\t`[previous-base, base_i)` per return frame and `[last-base, count)` for\n1439\tthe current activation, and needs a tail-completion seam to deliver a\n1440\ttail state through `K` (continuation design §4.3, slice 6c-pre); both\n1441\tkernels' positional frames become `E` through the owner chain and\n1442\t`bind-params`, with the task's free environment carried explicitly. The\n1443\tAST walker is not a frame reconstructor.\"\n1444\t\n1445\t**F4 — §10 phase 6 (ACCEPT).** Replace \"the row carrier amended\" with\n1446\t\"the row carrier amended to body version 3 with one profile,\n1447\t`{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`, carrying canonical vectors\n1448\tby A, `:yin.k/trees` and the task's free environment, never a native\n1449\timage (continuation design §2, §6)\"; after \"through their layouts\"\n1450\tinsert \"(the register and stack kernels, the latter with its\n1451\ttail-completion seam; the walker is excluded)\".\n1452\t\n1453\t### 10.2 To UCF (`yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md`)\n1454\t\n1455\t**U1 — §7.3.4 `:505-527` (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace `:511`\n1456\t\"`:yin.k/carried` carries vectors, not batches.\" with \"`:yin.k/carried`\n1457\tand the body's code map carry **register-shaped canonical vectors keyed\n1458\tby A**, never batches, never datoms projected from a vector, and never a\n1459\tnative stack or register image: a receiver of either native kernel\n1460\tderives its image from A (derivations design §2-3). `:yin.k/requires\n1461\t:yin.k/trees` maps every address in `:yin.k/segments` to the non-empty\n1462\tset of tree addresses the emitter's `source-index` held for it\n1463\t(derivations design §9.2).\" **Replace `:513-527`** (\"Loading a fetched\n1464\tvector has two paths … nothing may depend on which path a conforming\n1465\tengine takes.\") with: \"Loading a fetched vector has **one path**: the\n1466\tdirect decode of the canonical vector into an image through the one\n1467\tvalidator (`yin.vm.semantic-register.code/well-formed?`). The projection\n1468\tpath (vector → datoms → loader) is retired (owner ruling 2026-09-18;\n1469\t`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §3.4). The conformance obligation is\n1470\tthat the two AST projection lanes and the direct vector load yield one\n1471\timage and address (`load_paths_test.cljc`).\"\n1472\t\n1473\t**U2 — §7.4.1 (ACCEPT).** At its head: \"Superseded for the\n1474\tregister-shaped machine by `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §4.1 (two\n1475\tstate columns, `act` and `tail`, and the `deliver` record); the table\n1476\tbelow describes the stack-shaped machine, which leaves at that design's\n1477\tphase 8.\" Replace the `:yin.k/frame` example with §1.2's keyed form.\n1478\t\n1479\t**U3 — §7.4.2 (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace, in the opening\n1480\tparagraph, \"absolute stack depth and environment key sets at a pc depend\n1481\ton the *activation* — a closure enters with the caller's residual\n1482\toperand stack and an environment formed from its captured environment\n1483\tplus arguments (`apply-call`), and §2.6 enforces no equal stack heights\n1484\tat joins, so the same pc is legitimately reached at many depths\" with\n1485\t\"the saved window's values, the environment's bindings and the depth of\n1486\t`K` at a pc depend on the *activation*; the same pc is legitimately\n1487\treached under many windows and environments\". Replace \"E, St, and every\n1488\tK frame's `:stack-base` and env travel in the value\" with \"E, the saved\n1489\twindow, and every K frame's window, `rd` and env travel in the value, as\n1490\tdoes the task's free environment\". In the static map replace\n1491\t`[sp :yin.safepoint/stack-effect -1]` with `[sp :yin.safepoint/def #{…}]\n1492\t[sp :yin.safepoint/use #{…}] [sp :yin.safepoint/live #{…}]`; in the\n1493\trules replace \"`stack-effect` and `lexically-required` are derived from\n1494\tthe canonical vector alone, by the same static walk the linearizer\n1495\tperforms (§5.3). They are identical for every engine and checkable\n1496\tagainst the reference machine by a conformance test that runs the\n1497\tsegment to each safepoint and compares the observed deltas and E-reads.\n1498\tAbsolute depth, activation bases, captured environments, and physical\n1499\tlayouts are not claimed\" with \"`def`, `use`, `live` and\n1500\t`lexically-required` are derived from the canonical vector alone\n1501\t(`yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis`). They are identical for every\n1502\tengine and checkable against the reference machine by a conformance test\n1503\tthat runs the segment to each safepoint and compares the saved window's\n1504\tkey set with `live − {rd}` and the E-reads. Window values, environments,\n1505\t`K` and physical layouts are not claimed\"; replace \"physical slot →\n1506\tcanonical slot\" with \"physical location → virtual register\n1507\t(continuation design §4)\".\n1508\t\n1509\t**U4 — §7.4.3 (ACCEPT).** After \"Three rules make these resumable\":\n1510\t\"A pending rides on an `act` state (write-result delivery) or a `tail`\n1511\tstate (through-return delivery); the variants are unchanged, and\n1512\t`:yin.k/registers R` of the version-2 amendment is the `act`/`tail`\n1513\tstate of the frozen design §4.2.\"\n1514\t\n1515\t**U5 — §7.6 (ACCEPT).** In §7.6.1's example add\n1516\t`:yin.k/trees {A #{tree-address …}}  ; §7.6.1a` and a new §7.6.1a with\n1517\tthe phase-5 §9.2 UCF row text verbatim, including its completeness\n1518\tclause (absent or empty is incomplete).\n1519\t\n1520\t**U6 — §7.11 (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** In \"Safepoint conformance\n1521\tharness\" replace \"including `lift ∘ lower = id`, the static\n1522\t`stack-effect`/`lexically-required` checks\" with \"including `lift ∘\n1523\tlower = id` on canonical frames, the static `def`/`use`/`live` and\n1524\t`lexically-required` checks, the frame validator on every frame, and\n1525\t**cross-engine canonical equality**: one program at one safepoint lifts\n1526\tto row sets with equal root ids after the harness's specified\n1527\tre-emission (continuation design §5.5) from the semantic-register kernel\n1528\tand from the stack and register kernels through their layouts, the stack\n1529\tkernel with its tail-completion seam\". In §7.11.1 \"Safepoint\n1530\treconstruction\", replace \"Separately prepare two independently\n1531\timplemented UCF engines\" with \"Separately prepare the three engines\n1532\tintended to reconstruct canonical frames (the semantic-register kernel;\n1533\tthe register kernel; the stack kernel after its tail-completion seam)\"\n1534\tand \"the frame, pending wait, next result, and effect trace must agree\n1535\tin both directions\" with \"the canonical row set after re-emission, the\n1536\tpending wait, next result and effect trace must agree across all three\n1537\tand in every lowering direction\".\n1538\t\n1539\t### 10.3 To the row-carrier draft (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`)\n1540\t\n1541\tThe inventory below is every clause the grep of the draft for\n1542\t\"legacy\", \"version 0/1/2\", \"semantic profile only / semantic-only\",\n1543\t\"does not translate\", \"unchanged / do not move\", \"other profile\",\n1544\t\"registry\" found operative; each is replaced or deleted.\n1545\t\n1546\t**R1 — §2 `:50-81` (ACCEPT).** Replace the section with: \"**Body\n1547\tversion 3, one profile.** The carrier is body version 3 and reads no\n1548\tother version (owner, 2026-10-11: no legacy): a body of version 0, 1 or\n1549\t2 is `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` at the gate and is never normalised or\n1550\tupgraded. The profile map is `{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`;\n1551\tthere is no engine key, because the frame is the canonical\n1552\tregister-shaped machine's and the executing kernel is the receiving\n1553\tcomposition's choice: the stack and register kernels lower the same rows\n1554\tthrough their layouts (`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md`\n1555\t§2.1, §4). Any other profile map is `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`.\"\n1556\t\n1557\t**R1a — status paragraph `:18-20`.** Replace \"Body versions 0, 1 and 2\n1558\tkeep their grammar, readers and bytes; this document proposes a fourth\n1559\tbody version whose carrier is rows\" with \"This document specifies body\n1560\tversion 3, the one carrier; older bodies are not read.\"\n1561\t\n1562\t**R2 — §5.2 `:298-317` (ACCEPT).** Replace with continuation §2.3's\n1563\ttable and notes.\n1564\t\n1565\t**R3 — §5.1 `:287-296` (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace the `:reified`\n1566\trow with `| :reified | act-cref | a captured continuation: the decoded\n1567\tact state of frozen §4.2, no pending |`; replace \"`{:yin.k/tag\n1568\t:yin.k/frame :yin.k/registers R}`\" and \"`{:yin.k/tag :yin.k/frame\n1569\t:yin.k/parked-id P}`: resolves in the task's parked table; never\n1570\tduplicates `R`\" with the keyed `act` state and \"resolves in the task's\n1571\tparked table; never duplicates the state\"; replace \"A reified value's\n1572\tregisters are validated in captured-value context (amendment §7): its pc\n1573\tmust be a `:current-continuation` site's successor, not a wait or park\n1574\tsafepoint\" with \"A reified value's act is validated in context\n1575\t`:captured` (continuation §3.2 P3): its `pc−1` is a `:current-continuation`\n1576\tand it has no pending\"; and replace \"a reified value becomes a\n1577\treceiver-owned native continuation from `R`\" with \"from its act\".\n1578\t\n1579\t**R4 — §5.4 `:361` (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace `:parked-table |\n1580\tP₁ regs-cref₁ P₂ regs-cref₂ …` with `P₁ state-cref₁ …` (an `:act` or a\n1581\t`:tail`), and add: \"Validation of a parked state reads decoded task\n1582\tcontext, never an engine: the table key `P` and the set of call ids the\n1583\ttask's live `:ffi`/`:ffi-request` pendings carry are the `task` input of\n1584\t`frame/defect` (continuation §3.1), under which an `:act` at a `:park`\n1585\tsite is an explicit park and an `:act` at an `:ffi-call` site or a\n1586\t`:tail` at a tail call under a live call id is FFI bookkeeping.\"\n1587\t\n1588\t**R5 — §5.5 `:383-401` (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace the root with\n1589\tcontinuation §2.6 (adds `free-env-cref`; `contract` is the one profile\n1590\tmap; `code` is `{A \"v4\"-vector}`; `requires` gains `:yin.k/trees`); in\n1591\t`:394` replace \"`requires ; plain: UCF §7.6.1's map, unchanged`\" with\n1592\t\"`requires ; plain: UCF §7.6.1's map plus :yin.k/trees`\".\n1593\t\n1594\t**R6 — §8 step 7 `:661-667` (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace with:\n1595\t\"**Frames.** Every `:act`, `:tail`, `:kframe`, `:reified` and\n1596\tparked-table state is decoded to its keyed frame and judged by\n1597\t`yin.vm.semantic-register.frame/defect` with its context (`:wait`,\n1598\t`:captured`, `:parked`) and the decoded task context (parked key, live\n1599\tFFI call ids, the root's free environment); a defect is\n1600\t`:yin.k/undecodable` with the rule's kind and the row path (continuation\n1601\t§3). This step runs after canonical numbering (step 6) and before\n1602\tpending validation (step 8).\"\n1603\t\n1604\t**R6a — §8 step 1 `:618-623`.** Replace \"then every profile map against\n1605\tthe registry (only the semantic profile is supported, §2)\" with \"then\n1606\tevery profile map against the one profile map of §2\".\n1607\t\n1608\t**R7 — `:63-68` and §10.4 `:774-777` (ACCEPT).** Delete \"Code stamps\n1609\t`\"v3\"`, `\"b2\"`, `\"r2\"` and the inner version 1 do not move: this is a\n1610\tchange of carrier, not of instruction, scheduler, or value semantics,\n1611\texactly the distinction the amendment draws between its versions and\n1612\texecutable code.\" Replace §10.4 with: \"**Contract stamp.** The code\n1613\tcontract carried is `\"v4\"`, the register-shaped machine's; the carrier\n1614\tversion is 3; the two are independent, and neither names a legacy\n1615\tvalue.\"\n1616\t\n1617\t**R8 — §9 `:737-746` \"Legacy correspondence\" and §10.8 `:797-801`\n1618\t(ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Delete both: there is no legacy reader and no\n1619\tnormalisation tool. In §10.3 `:769-773` delete \"Versions 0, 1 and 2\n1620\tremain compatibility inputs. One canonical nested projection of version\n1621\t3 is kept for single-message channels and must stay exactly mutually\n1622\tinverse with the rows.\" and \"Retiring old readers is an owner\n1623\tversion-support decision\", leaving \"Rows are the carrier authority.\"\n1624\tIn §9's law list delete \"Exact mutual inversion is required only between\n1625\tversion 3 and its one canonical nested projection (§10.3)\".\n1626\t\n1627\t**R9 — §10.6 `:782-788`, §10.7 `:792-796`, §2 `:70-81`, §10's\n1628\tproposals list `:821-834`, \"Still open\" `:836-837`, §11 `:839-852`\n1629\t(ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** §10.6, **whole item**: replace its opening\n1630\t\"**Foreign-engine value profiles.** Required before any implementation\n1631\tbrief claims heterogeneous execution conformance, and not drafted here\"\n1632\twith \"**Foreign-engine value profiles.** Required before an\n1633\timplementation brief claims execution conformance for an engine\n1634\t**outside the three repository lanes** (the semantic-register kernel and\n1635\tthe stack and register kernels, whose reconstruction is the layouts of\n1636\t`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §4 and needs no value\n1637\tprofile), and not drafted here\"; keep its list of what such a profile\n1638\tmust cover; and replace \"version 3, like version 2, does\n1639\tnot translate between kernels\" with \"version 3 carries the canonical\n1640\tframe; a stack or register kernel reconstructs it through its layout\n1641\t(continuation §4), which is heterogeneous reconstruction, not\n1642\ttranslation between native formats; foreign-engine *value* profiles for\n1643\tengines outside this repository remain a separate document\". §10.7:\n1644\tdelete (\"there are no other profile tables\"). Proposals list: delete\n1645\t\"semantic-only initial scope\"; add \"one engine-less profile (continuation\n1646\t§2.1)\" and \"the explicit root `free-env` (§6.3)\". \"Still open\": replace\n1647\twith \"none beyond the work-bound limits (§10.10)\". §11: replace \"Code\n1648\tidentity, the contract stamp and profile registry, safepoints,\" with\n1649\t\"Code identity (A), safepoints,\"; delete \"versions 0-2\" references.\n1650\t\n1651\t**R10 — §5.5 `:421-426` custody paragraph.** Replace \"a version-3 fork\n1652\troot is admitted exactly as a version-0 body is, proposes nothing, and\n1653\tis never upgraded to custody\" with \"a fork root proposes nothing and is\n1654\tnever upgraded to custody; an exclusive-only receiver refuses it as\n1655\t`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`\".\n1656\t\n1657\t**R11 — §3 `:115-134`.** Keep verbatim, including \"**body version 3\n1658\tuses BLAKE3 permanently**\" and the per-id algorithm check (the reviewer\n1659\tasked that this explicit rule survive).\n1660\t\n1661\t**U7 — scope and precedence of UCF's historical legacy-body clauses\n1662\t(new).** UCF keeps clauses that describe bodies the row carrier never\n1663\treads: §7.2.1 (versions 0 and 1, `:166-321`), the version-0/1 custody\n1664\tgate and fork rules (`:234-290`), §7.4.3 r5's version-0 notes (`:966-970`:\n1665\t\"A version-0 entry without a phase reads as `:running`\", \"The landed\n1666\tversion-0 reader breaches both\"), §7.7.4's `nil`-header version-0 lift\n1667\tand recovery of legacy fork bytes (`:1781`, `:1806-1807`, `:1844`), and\n1668\t§7.11.1's version-0/1 interoperation rows (`:3051-3057`, `:3095-3096`).\n1669\tInsert at the head of §7.2.1: \"**Scope (2026-10-11).** Body versions 0,\n1670\t1 and 2 and every clause of this document that admits, reads, recovers\n1671\tor interoperates with them are **historical**: they describe the\n1672\tstack-shaped machine's handoff, which leaves at\n1673\t`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §10 phase 8. The row carrier of body\n1674\tversion 3 (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md` as amended by\n1675\t`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md`) reads no other version and\n1676\ttakes **precedence** over any sentence below that implies otherwise; a\n1677\tconflict is resolved in its favour without further amendment. **Not\n1678\thistorical**: the custody, fencing and operation-id semantics (§7.7.8,\n1679\t§7.9, §7.4.3's operation ids) travel in version 3 as the root's\n1680\t`custody` slot (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md` §5.5) and stay\n1681\toperative; where those sections say 'a version-1 body' read, for version\n1682\t3, 'a root whose custody policy is `:yin.k/exclusive`', and where they\n1683\tsay 'a version-0 body' or 'fork', 'a root whose policy is `:yin.k/fork`'\n1684\t(§5.5's table). The code stamp `{:yin.code/contract \"v3\" :yin.k/version\n1685\t0}` wherever this document shows it (§7.2's example `:121`, §7.2.1\n1686\t`:183`, §7.3.3 `:232-236`) is the stack-shaped machine's; the\n1687\tregister-shaped machine's contract is `\"v4\"`\n1688\t(`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §6), the one the version-3 profile map\n1689\tnames, and §7.2's envelope example is superseded for version 3 by the\n1690\trow carrier's wire unit (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md` §3, ids under\n1691\tJing's default digest).\" The same grep (`legacy`, `version-0`,\n1692\t`version 0`, `versions 0`, `version 1`, `recovery`) found, besides the\n1693\tclauses above: the export-recovery object's version-1 format\n1694\t(`:1789-1807`), which is phase 7's to re-base on the row carrier and is\n1695\tnamed in §8.4 as an entry condition, not amended here; publication\n1696\tfailure recovery (`:1741`), completion recovery (`:2417`) and the\n1697\tledger's \"legacy destructive readers\" (`:2774-2775`), which concern the\n1698\tdriver, the ledger protocol and the ledger reader, not a body version,\n1699\tand are untouched; and the status paragraph `:39-42`, covered by the\n1700\tscope statement's \"every clause\".\n1701\t\n1702\t### 10.4 To code-as-tuples (`yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`) §7.2\n1703\t\n1704\t**C1 (ACCEPT).** Replace the first paragraph with: \"The vector-to-datoms\n1705\tprojection path is **retired** (owner ruling 2026-09-18; frozen §3.4\n1706\t'One vector validator'). There is one load path for a vector, the direct\n1707\tone, and two AST projection lanes (datom lane, row lane) that produce\n1708\tthe vector; all three feed one validator\n1709\t(`yin.vm.semantic-register.code/well-formed?`). UCF §7.3.4's projection\n1710\tpath is superseded accordingly.\" Replace obligation 2's second sentence\n1711\twith \"loading the vector produced by either AST lane and the vector\n1712\tloaded directly yield the same image and address (`load_paths_test.cljc`)\",\n1713\tand obligation 3's \"both paths refuse with the same defect\" with \"the\n1714\tdirect vector load refuses with the published defect (rule and pc) for\n1715\tevery rule of the frozen §3.4\". Obligations 1 and 4 stand.\n1716\t\n1717\t### 10.5 Checked and consistent (no amendment)\n1718\t\n1719\tFrozen §2.4 delivery shapes against the 4b branch; frozen §4.1 two state\n1720\tcolumns; the evaluator design §1.3-1.6; the draft's §3, §4, §5.1 (except\n1721\t`:reified`), §5.3, §6, §7 and §8 steps 1-6, 8-12; v2 amendment §2's `E`\n1722\tshape; the phase-5 §9.2 `:yin.k/trees` text; the register kernel's\n1723\t`:return-result` delivery (`register.cljc:458-468`).\n1724\t\n1725\t---\n1726\t\n1727\t## 11. Owner questions\n1728\t\n1729\t**None.** The reviewer accepted the engine-less profile and rejected the\n1730\tmerged-`E` free environment; both are now settled in the text. Nothing\n1731\tremaining is owner-level.\n1732\t\n1733\t---\n1734\t\n1735\t## 12. Portability notes for the implementer\n1736\t\n1737\t1. **Nil-valued window keys (Dart, Node).** The window is built with\n1738\t   `select-keys` and encoded as `[r [:lit nil]]`; never filter `some?`\n1739\t   values; `frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member` over row 22\n1740\t   (`(pair nil (next-of c))`, the nil operand evaluated before the read)\n1741\t   is the canary. Membership is always by `contains?`/key sets, never\n1742\t   `(get W r)`.\n1743\t2. **`for` over large seqs (Dart).** Row sets of the C4 modules run to\n1744\t   thousands of rows; build with `mapv`/`into`/`reduce`.\n1745\t3. **Reader whitespace before closers (Dart).** Pinned row sets are\n1746\t   Clojure data in `.cljc`, never EDN strings.\n1747\t4. **Duplicate protocol params (Dart).** `gc-children [_ _x]`\n1748\t   (`srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:386`); any new protocol method\n1749\t   in `layout` likewise.\n1750\t5. **Multi-key `assoc` on nil (Dart).** Frames and windows start from\n1751\t   `{}` (`handoff.cljc:1455-1457` records the trap).\n1752\t6. **Reader conditionals.** `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)`\n1753\t   with `:cljd` first; `:clj`-only source-reading tests as `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)`.\n1754\t7. **Private var access (Dart).** Every function named in §8 is public;\n1755\t   no `#'`.\n1756\t8. **Sorted keys.** Window and bindings rows are sorted by Jing\n1757\t   canonical bytes of the key, never by host `sort` on mixed types.\n1758\t9. **Numeric classes (Node).** `pc`, `rd`, `r`, `site` are exact\n1759\t   integers; compare with `cbor/numeric-kind` before `=` on wire values\n1760\t   (`ucf/profile-engine`, `ucf.cljc:77-91`, is the template).\n1761\t10. **Fresh worktree.** `mise trust` and `npm ci` before the Node lane.\n1762\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02df6bdc-04b9-48af-9b17-9798293c08e5","uuid":"58966d5c-0e2e-44fd-8c00-3450c2d5d653","timestamp":"2026-10-12T17:42:08.724Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-6b-amend/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md","content":"| 19 | halt | `(lit 42)` | — | result | `42` | yes |\n| 20 | **tail-effect halt** | run **outside the wrappers**, in two batches on one machine: a setup batch `(then (def! 's (stream/make 4)) (def! 'c (cursor-of s)))` run to halt (store writes persist across batches, as `lift_support.cljc:320-322` relies on), then the batch `(stream/next! c)` **marked `:tail? true` at the root**, `c` resolving through the store; no application precedes the call, so `K` is empty (any `let1` or wrapper would push a frame, §5.2 above) | append `\"B\"` | tail, `:next` | halts with `\"B\"` (4b: a tail effect with no frame to pop halts, `srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:205-211` stage 2; stack: the seam's empty-`K` case, §4.3), env free of `store-of` | yes |\n| 21 | **free-env shadowing** (the review's row) | initial free env `{x 99}`; `(let1 f (fn [] x) ((fn [x] (f (next-of c))) 1))` | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next`; `E` at the read binds `x` to 1; root `free-env` carries `x 99` | the lowered `f` returns `99` (not nil, not 1) on every lane; **the one row the earlier design would have failed** | yes |\n| 22 | nil-valued live register | `(let1 pair (fn [p q] (cat (cat [] p) q)) (pair nil (next-of c)))`: the `nil` operand is evaluated **before** the read and is live across it (`(cat nil (next-of c))` would give `(conj nil \"B\")`, the list `(\"B\")`, so a vector-building `pair` is used; there is no `vector` primitive, `vm.cljc:380-410`, and `pair` builds through the segment's `cat`) | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next`; `W` has a present key with `[:lit nil]` | `[nil \"B\"]` | yes |\n| 23 | tail FFI bookkeeping | a `tail` parked record under a call id `P ∈ :ffi-call-ids` | — | parked, context `:parked`, bookkeeping clause of P4 | validator accepts; the **same valid tail under a key not in `:ffi-call-ids`** is `:parked-site` (P4); moving `site` to a non-tail call is `:site` (T1, which runs first) | **synthetic**: no primitive returns an FFI effect through a tail `:call` today (evaluator §1.6) |\n| 24 | `act` FFI bookkeeping | 3's parked bookkeeping record under its call id | — | parked, P4 bookkeeping | validator accepts | 4b stage 2 |\n\nRefusal rows: `:yin.k/not-quiescent` (`a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-not-quiescent`,\n`:591-603`); `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` (a register kernel stepped one\ninstruction past a `:const`, asked to lift); `:yin.k/non-portable\n:reason-mismatch` (the `:observe` hold, `:675-692`); and the validator's\n**membership tampers**, each a row-set edit of a valid body before\nlower: a window with an extra live key → `:window-extra`; a live key\nremoved → `:window-missing`; `rd` added → `:window-self`; `rd` replaced\nby another register → `:destination`; a return frame's `pc` moved after\na tail call → `:return-site`; a reason the site does not admit →\n`:reason-mismatch`; a `:tail` row given a fourth slot → `:frame-shape`;\nthe `[:lit nil]` of row 22 dropped → `:window-missing`; a `:reified`\nact whose `pc−1` is not a capture → `:captured-site`; a parked act whose\n`pc−1` is not `:park` → `:parked-site`; for E2, with row 21's initial\nfree environment extended to `{x 99 y 7}`, the **unshadowed** free\nbinding `y` in the act's `E` changed to `8` → `:free-env-mismatch`\n(changing the lexical `x`, which is `1` at the read, trips nothing: E2\ncompares off the lexical names), and the lexical `x` **removed** from\n`E` → `:free-env-mismatch` (presence clause (a)); the root `free-env`\nrow given a reserved key → `:reserved-name` (X1). **A changed live value**\n(e.g. `\"A\"` → `\"Z\"` in row 1's window) is not a membership defect and is\nnot expected to be refused: it is tested by **execution parity** (the\nlowered run's result differs from the reference), as the review ruled.\n\n### 5.3 Lanes\n\nThe `:semantic-register` lane's wait entries are canonical frames plus\nengine fields. The de Bruijn lanes load `(:image (derive/stack-image v))`\nand `(:image (derive/register-image v))` of `v = (:vector (project P))`\nthrough `dvm/create-vm`/`rvm/create-vm`, run to the safepoint and lift\nthrough `layout/lift-act`/`lift-tail`; the stack lane's tail rows (6,\n9, 12, 20) require the seam of §4.3 and are gated on 6c-pre.\n\n### 5.4 Laws\n\n1. **Reference parity**: result and effect trace of the lowered,\n   satisfied machine equal the reference run (`reference`/`handed-off`,\n   `:368-401`).\n2. **Round trip**: `lift(lower(S)) = S` by root id under the\n   fresh-receiver context of the draft's §9, after the re-emission of\n   §5.5.\n3. **Observed reason**: the pending's reason is the wait's, never the\n   static kind (ucf-revisions §8).\n4. **Cross-engine canonical equality**: one program at one safepoint\n   lifts to row sets whose root ids are **equal after the re-emission of\n   §5.5** on all three lanes.\n5. **Cross-engine lowering**: a row set lifted on one lane lowers on\n   each of the other two (six ordered pairs) and continues to the\n   reference result.\n6. **Validator agreement**: every lifted frame passes `frame/defect` in\n   its context; every tamper of §5.2 is refused with its kind; the\n   verdict is lane-independent.\n\n### 5.5 Re-emission for equality (replacing \"stream-blinding\")\n\n**PROPOSED** (reviewer: `stream-blind` rewrites decoded maps and does\nnot recompute Merkle ids, so it cannot establish root-id equality). The\nharness first **fixes identities where it can**: all three lanes serve\ntheir streams through one toy channel (`v2_support/toy`,\n`served-peer`), so stream identities and descriptors are equal across\nlanes by construction where the same logical stream is lifted. Where a\nlane mints its own (fresh cursor cells on relift, the receiver's own call\npair), the comparison uses `rows/canonical-under`, a **test-only**\ntransformation whose placeholder assignment is **never derived from\n*host* traversal order** (the canonical walk of draft §6 is a function\nof the state and is what the procedure reads; the review's objection: map and set traversal, and\n\"cursor cells by body\", can depend on the very identities being erased). It\ntakes an **explicit logical-stream correspondence** from the fixture:\nthe harness created every stream the row reaches, so it supplies\n`{lane-identity → logical-name}` (e.g. `{id-of-s :s, id-of-call-out\n:call-out}`) for each lane; `canonical-under` decodes the row set to the\nabstract task (draft §6's input), replaces each stream marker's identity\nand descriptor by the logical name the map gives it (a marker the map\ndoes not cover is a test failure, never a guess), runs the canonical\ncursor-cell numbering (draft §6), re-emits every row and recomputes every id,\nand compares root ids. Draft §6 is invariant under renaming of the\n**cursor cells** (its labels never encode an incoming cursor-cell id), and the only\nother identity it consumes is the stream marker in each cursor cell's body\nlabel (`[:body [:stream identity descriptor] position]`, draft §6 as\namended, spelled by rank inside keys) and in cursor-cell bodies; after the substitution those are the fixture's\nlogical names, so the procedure's inputs no longer depend on any lane's\nidentities. Guest sets and maps are entered in the bytewise order of\ntheir members' keys, and `:store`, `:bindings` and the parked table in\nthe byte order of their structural keys (draft §6 W1), never in host\nenumeration order, so\na permutation of the erased identities cannot change the result once\nthe markers are substituted. It is never used outside the harness.\n\n### 5.6 Static checks the harness runs once per corpus segment\n\n1. `frame/defect` on every frame the reference lane mints: nil.\n2. For every **reachable** parking pc `p` of `v`: `(analysis/saved a\n   (inc p) rd)` has no member `≥ k(body(p))` and does not contain `rd`.\n3. Register layout: at every reachable boundary pc `p`, `virt(p, s)` is\n   single-valued on the physical image of `live-out*(p)`; the `live`\n   operand of `R[p]` equals `(sort (map phys (disj live-out*(p) rd)))`,\n   the destination removed as a **virtual** id before mapping, which is\n   `[]` for a tail call (phase-5 §2.5). Worked example, inner call at\n   `p = 3`: `L(4) = {1 2}`, minus `rd 2` → `{1}` → `[0]`, the pinned\n   `live` of phase-5 §6.3 row 2.\n4. Stack layout: the k-th non-push instruction of `H` has the mnemonic\n   family of `v[k]` for every `k`; counts agree.\n5. Stack layout: `(set (stack-layout p)) = (analysis/saved a (inc p)\n   rd)` for every reachable **non-tail** parking pc `p`.\n6. `E` reconstruction: at every safepoint reached, the layout's `E`\n   equals the reference lane's `E` (values normalised), including rows\n   21 and 22 and the `:duplicate-param`, `:nested-closure`,\n   `:nested-lambdas` programs.\n7. Closure reconstruction: canonical ↔ positional closures round-trip on\n   the `\"closure value\"` and `\"higher order\"` B0 rows and\n   `:duplicate-param`.\n8. Tail lowering: the `:frames`/`:store-of` chosen for a lowered `tail`\n   entry are unobservable: lowering with `[]`/`nil` and with arbitrary\n   values gives equal observables on rows 6, 9, 12, 20.\n9. Slices: for every non-tail safepoint with `m` return frames, the\n   `m+1` slices of §4.3 partition the stack kernel's operand stack\n   exactly, and each has the length of its `stack-layout`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Code and task context in the carrier\n\n### 6.1 Code\n\n**DECIDED** (rulings 1, 3, 4; phase-5 §7.6, §9.2; v2 amendment §4's\n2026-10-10 note). The root's `code` slot is plain `{A canonical-vector}`\nof `\"v4\"` vectors, verified to hash to their key and to pass\n`code/well-formed?`. **No native image travels**: a stack or register\nreceiver derives `H(A)`/`R(A)` with `derive/stack-image`/`register-image`.\n`requires` carries UCF §7.6.1's map **plus** `:yin.k/trees {A #{tree-address …}}`,\none entry per address in `:yin.k/segments`; the **complete association\nrule** is phase-5's: an absent entry **or an empty set** is incomplete\n(`:yin.k/missing :yin.k/trees`, discovery `:incomplete`), and a claimed\naddress alone does not establish retrievability (a known address whose\nread fails now is the medium's `:absent`, not a missing association).\n\n### 6.2 Rows, not datoms\n\n**DECIDED** (ruling 4). No vector is projected to datoms; the direct\nload path is the only path (§10.4).\n\n### 6.3 The free environment: carrier, source, ownership\n\n**DECIDED** by the review's finding and §4.4. The task's initial free\nenvironment travels **once, explicitly**, as the root's `free-env`\nslot, a `:bindings` row (`[S V …]` sorted). Every `E` in the task is a\ncomplete map and is checked by rules X1 and E2. On lower, the\nsemantic-register kernel receives it as the machine's base `:env`\n(`create-vm`'s `:env` option, `semantic_register.cljc:261`); a de Bruijn\nkernel receives it as its `:free-env` (`stack.cljc:418`) and\nreconstructs positional frames from each `E` by the chain (§4.4).\n\n**Where the lift gets it (PROPOSED, the gap the review named).** It is\n**never recovered from a current `E`** (§4.4). Its source is, per\nkernel:\n\n- **de Bruijn kernels**: the kernel's own `:free-env` field, \"fixed for\n  this instance\" (`stack.cljc:82`; `register.cljc:50`), read directly.\n- **the semantic-register kernel**: the evaluator keeps only the\n  mutable-current `:env` (`RegisterVM` field `env`, \"persistent lexical\n  scope map\", `srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:23`; the old semantic\n  VM likewise captures the initial env only transiently in `eval`,\n  `semantic.cljc:874-876`), so no field holds the initial map. The\n  **composition owns it**: it is the value the composition passed as\n  `create-vm`'s `:env` (`vm/check-bindings!` of it, `:261`). The lift's\n  input contract therefore takes it explicitly,\n  `(rows/lift-task vm serve! {:free-env E₀})`, and refuses\n  `:yin.k/non-portable :missing-free-env` when the caller supplies none;\n  the holder and REPL paths that call the lift pass the environment they\n  constructed the task with. **Coordinated retention seam, recommended**:\n  4b (stage 3, its track's file) adds an immutable `free-env` field set\n  once in `create-vm` from the checked `:env` and never written by any\n  transition, with `gc-roots` listing it; once it lands the lift reads\n  it when `:free-env` is not supplied and the explicit argument stays as\n  the override for compositions that constructed the task elsewhere.\n  Phase 6 does **not** edit `semantic_register.cljc`; 6b depends on the\n  explicit argument and names the seam as a follow-up (§8.2).\n\nMerkle sharing means every `E` whose bindings equal another's shares one\n`:bindings` row; the root slot is one more reference to a row that\nusually already exists.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Lift and lower\n\n### 7.1 Lift\n\n**DECIDED** (draft §9, UCF §7.8): refuse unless quiescent; refuse the\nholds (`unliftable-hold`, `handoff.cljc:588`) as `:yin.k/non-portable\n:reason-mismatch`; classify kind; run the **dependency closure over the\n`\"v4\"` vectors**, which needs the phase-5 scanners\n(`scan/requirements`, `scan/free-names`, `scan/free-occurrences` over the\n§2.3 table: the current `completion/code-facts` reads stack-table\npositions and cannot be used), and refuse `:yin.k/unsatisfied` unless\n`:complete`, `:yin.k/trees` included; number cursor cells (draft §6); walk\nwaits, parked records, the store slice, module stores, the free\nenvironment (from the kernel's `:free-env` field or the lift's explicit\n`:free-env` argument, §6.3, never from a current `E`), the result,\ninstall children; run `frame/defect` over every\nframe; emit rows and the census. A de Bruijn source walks the frames\n`layout/lift-act`/`lift-tail` reconstruct.\n\n### 7.2 Lower\n\n**DECIDED** (draft §8 in order; §3.3): gate, structure, graph, hashes,\ncanonical form, canonical numbering, **frames**, pending and operations,\ndependency closure (`requires`/`code` agree with the census;\n`:yin.k/trees` complete per §6.1), custody, composition, restore. Restore\nbuilds the receiving kernel's state: semantic-register: `code` through\n`load-vector`/`attach-image` under `code/contract`, the free environment\nas base `:env`, each `:wait` to an engine entry (payload plus the\npending's engine fields, `lower-frame!`'s shapes, `handoff.cljc:3182-3246`,\n`:deliver` carried), parked records into `:parked`, the result into\n`:value`; de Bruijn: derive and attach the image for each A, set\n`:free-env`, and `layout/lower-act`/`lower-tail` each frame (the stack\nlane's `tail` needs 6c-pre). Restoration delivers nothing, runs nothing,\nmints nothing.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Slices, gates, entry conditions\n\nVerification follows `docs/agents/build-n-test.md`: G0 per iteration on\nthe JVM, G1 `bb test:sub yin.vm` on three hosts, G2 `bb test:changed`,\nG3 on master.\n\n### 8.1 Slice 6a: the frame validator and the row codec (independent)\n\n**Files to create.**\n- `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc` (§3): `defect`, public.\n- `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` (§2): the row table as data,\n  `frame->rows`, `rows->frame`, row ids (Jing default), the census and\n  numbering per the draft §6, `canonical-under` (§5.5, test-only but\n  placed here so three test namespaces share it). **Not** `lift-task`/\n  `lower-task`: full task transport is 6b.\n- `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame_test.cljc`,\n  `test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc`.\n\n**Depends on:** phase 3, 4a (landed), 4b stage 1 (branch) for live\nframes to validate. Touches nothing of 4b or 5; needs no scanner.\n\n**Acceptance (6a).**\n\n1. `frame-test/contract-is-pure`: `frame/defect` takes `[frame code\n   context task]`, `task` being plain data; the namespace's `ns` form\n   requires no kernel and no `yin.vm.engine` (a string check over the\n   source on the JVM lane, `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)`).\n2. `frame-test/every-reference-frame-validates`: for every 4b-stage-1\n   row of §5.2 (1, 2, 5, 6, 13-16, 18, 19, 21, 22) over the four segments,\n   plus row 20 as one separate, unwrapped run (its empty `K` needs no wrapper\n   frames; §8.2 6b makes the same exception), every\n   `act`, `tail`, return frame, parked record and reified value the\n   register evaluator mints passes `defect` in its context with the\n   task context decoded from the machine's own tables.\n3. `frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper`: for each rule S1-S4, C1-C3,\n   A1-A6, T1, K1-K3, E1-E2, X1, P1-P4 one tampered frame built from a\n   valid one, refused with that rule's kind and a path naming the slot\n   (**twenty-four rules**: 4+3+6+1+3+2+1+4, the twenty-three of the\n   round-1 text plus X1; **twenty-five rows**, since C2 contributes two,\n   a float `pc` for `:pc-kind` and an out-of-range one for `:pc-bounds`;\n   X1's row goes through `frame/task-defect`); plus\n   `first-defect-is-structural`: a frame with a malformed `K` **and** a\n   bad window reports `:k-shape`.\n4. `frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member`: row 22's frame\n   validates with the nil key present; the same frame with the key\n   removed is `:window-missing`.\n5. `frame-test/worked-example-saved`: on `:worked-example`, a frame at pc\n   4 with window `{1 <f>}` and `rd 2` validates; `{1 <f> 2 x}` is\n   `:window-self`; `{}` is `:window-missing`; `{1 <f> 3 x}` is\n   `:window-extra` (`saved(4, 2) = {1}`, `analysis_test.cljc:131-139`).\n6. `frame-test/free-env-mismatch`: row 21's frame (initial free\n   environment `{x 99 y 7}`) with `task :free-env {x 99 y 7}` validates;\n   with the free environment `{x 99 y 8}` or `{x 99}` it is\n   `:free-env-mismatch` (`y` is unshadowed); with the lexical `x` removed\n   from `E` it is `:free-env-mismatch` (presence); changing the lexical\n   `x` in `E` from `1` to `98` **does not** trip E2 (it is off the\n   comparison), and the test asserts that too; a `free-env` row with the\n   key `yin/def` is `:reserved-name` (X1).\n7. `rows-test/bijection`: `frame->rows ∘ rows->frame` and the converse\n   are identities on every frame of item 2, nil-valued keys included.\n8. `rows-test/row-ids-are-jing-default`: every content row's id equals\n   `(jing/segment-key body)` and names Jing's default algorithm; no\n   `sha256` appears in any id.\n9. `rows-test/window-sorted-and-unique`: an out-of-order or duplicated\n   `:window` row is `:yin.k/undecodable` at canonical form (step 5).\n10. `rows-test/canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`: §5.5's\n    transformation gives equal root ids for two emissions of one abstract\n    task under permuted cursor-cell numbering and distinct stream identities,\n    with the fixture's correspondence map; **and the unordered-container\n    permutation**: a store value that is a set of two stream references\n    and a map keyed by two cursor references, emitted twice with the two\n    streams' identities swapped (and the correspondence map swapped\n    accordingly), gives equal root ids; a marker absent from the map is\n    a test failure.\n11. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts; Node log\n    shows `Testing yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test` and\n    `Testing yin.vm.ucf.rows-test`.\n12. `rows-test/discovery-order-numbering`: `canonical-numbering` returns\n    the maps of the numbering note's appendix A for `fixture :s1 :s2 :x\n    :y`, the review counterexample, `[x x y]`, `[x y y]`, `[#{X Y} X]`,\n    the witness `[#{#{[A B] [B A]}} A]`, `[#{X Y} #{Y Z}]`, the path and\n    the two frame fixtures.\n13. `rows-test/occurrence-count-separates-members`: the review\n    counterexample numbers `Y cc-1, X cc-2`, pinned `2d9873a8…`; the path\n    pinned `726a9fbb…`; `[#{X Y} #{Y Z}]` pinned `d84480d4…`; each equal\n    after renaming plus reversal of every set.\n14. `rows-test/interchangeable-ties`: `#{X Y}`, `#{[X X] [Y Y]}`,\n    `{X 1, Y 1}`, `#{#{X Y} #{Z W}}` number without refusal; reversal and\n    renaming give equal roots; pins `07eda35d…`, `da69c679…`,\n    `49d4478c…`, `18b70de6…`.\n15. `rows-test/alias-pattern-is-part-of-the-key`: `#{[X X] [Y Z]}` and\n    `{X X, Y Z}` give one root for both enumerations and after renaming,\n    pinned `387f294a…` and `be62ba43…`; the witness numbers `B cc-1,\n    A cc-2`, pinned `0193312…`, and decodes; the balanced-alias witness\n    `#{[X X Y Y] [Z W Z W]}` gives one root for both enumerations, pinned\n    `5376f133…`, and the key without the local index would not.\n16. `rows-test/unresolved-cursor-cells-refuse`: the 2-cycle, the\n    3-cycle, the loop plus 2-cycle, the seven-cell state,\n    `[#{X Y} #{X Y}]`, the mixed-body, the anchored, the two-2-cycle and\n    the 3-cycle-beside-fan states refuse at `emit` with\n    `:yin.k/non-portable :unresolved-cursor-cells`, the paths and cells of\n    the numbering note's appendix A, the same verdict and path after\n    renaming plus shuffling; a carrier of each built with `emit-numbered`\n    decodes to `:yin.k/undecodable :unresolved-cursor-cells` with the\n    path prefixed by the root, never `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`; a\n    parent whose install `'a` holds the 2-cycle refuses at `emit` with\n    path `[12 a 15]` and its `emit-numbered` carrier decodes to the\n    `:yin.k/undecodable` kind with path `[<root> 12 a 15]`.\n17. `rows-test/canonical-roots-are-pinned`: `fab223…` and `c4a7c7…`\n    unchanged; `a850fce6…` (`[#{X Y} X]`), `4993b5b1…`, `536c810b…`,\n    `e67405ec…` (`[#{#{X Y} #{Z W}} X]`), `6e7c7a6b…` (ten cells) added;\n    `55ff168e…` removed.\n18. `rows-test/counterexample-search`: a seeded generator (at least 2000\n    random value states, 200 frame-bearing, 100 with install children)\n    in CI: every numbered state's carrier decodes and re-emits to its\n    root; renaming every cursor cell plus shuffling every set, map and\n    census gives an equal root, or the same refusal verdict and path;\n    refusals are counted and reported; the largest `:work` is reported.\n19. `rows-test/numbering-is-total`: a census cell the walk does not reach\n    raises the totality defect, not a refusal, before any row is emitted.\n20. `numbering-precedes-frame-defect`, `alias-topology-and-census`,\n    `canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`,\n    `unordered-containers-are-order-free`,\n    `child-scope-and-shared-child-dag` and\n    `census-is-numeric-from-ten-cursor-cells` pass unchanged against the\n    rewritten decoder; `numbering-precedes-frame-defect` is extended: the\n    2-cycle with the same reserved-name binding, carried by\n    `emit-numbered`, decodes to `:yin.k/undecodable\n    :unresolved-cursor-cells`, not `:reserved-name`.\n21. `rows-test/gates-and-work`: 65 cells refuse `:resource-limit\n    [:cursor-cells]` under the default budget and 2 cells under\n    `{:cursor-cells 1}`; `[[[[X]]]]` under `{:depth 3}` refuses\n    `[:depth]`, and so do one cell inside 3000 nested vectors under\n    `{:depth 3}` and under the default budget, and a literal nested 3000\n    deep beside a cell (no host stack overflow on any of the three hosts;\n    200 nested vectors number); a set holding a 400000-scalar literal\n    refuses `[:work]` under `{:work 2000}` with the work counter at 2001\n    and under `{:work 900000}` with at most 1000 estimator steps; a state\n    whose bodies carry a 65536-character descriptor numbers under the\n    default budget; `{:work 1}` refuses `[:work]` at `emit` and, for a\n    valid carrier, at `decode`.\n22. Budgets: `:label-bytes` and `:search` gone, `:work` default\n    `4194304`.\n\n### 8.2 Slice 6b: full task transport and the harness on the reference lane\n\n**Files to change.** `rows.cljc`: `lift-task`, `lower-task` (§7), the\npending rows' lift and lower, install children. **Files to create.**\n`test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc` (§5, the\n`:semantic-register` lane). The old harness file is not edited.\n\n**Depends on:** the explicit `:free-env` lift argument supplied by the\nharness (§6.3; the 4b retention seam is a named follow-up for the 4b\ntrack, not a 6b prerequisite); 4b stage 2 (FFI retained→sent restoration, link\nrequest/response/install preservation, install children, the\nevaluator's `IModuleKernel` linking methods: `link-format`,\n`spawn-module`, `lift-closure`, `lower-closure`); **phase 5c** (the\n`scan` namespace, for the dependency closure over `\"v4\"` vectors, §7.1).\nTouches nothing of 4b or 5.\n\n**Acceptance (6b).**\n\n1. `every-row-every-segment-matches-the-reference`: rows 1-19, 21, 22\n   and 24 of §5.2 × four segments, plus row 20 once (outside the\n   wrappers, §5.2), on the reference lane; laws 1-3 and 6; counts\n   asserted (22 wrapped rows × 4 segments + 1 = 89 runs).\n2. `tail-states-carry-no-window`: rows 6, 9, 12, 20 lift to `:tail`\n   rows of three slots and lower to through-`K` delivery.\n3. `install-rows-carry-the-child`: rows 10-12; the child's kind and\n   phase as stated; no initialization on lower.\n4. `captures`: rows 14-16 round-trip; row 15's invocation after lower\n   delivers once into the captured `rd` and yields `:done`.\n5. `free-env-shadowing`: row 21 yields `99` after lower.\n6. `synthetic-tail-bookkeeping`: row 23's hand-built parked `tail`\n   under a call id in `:ffi-call-ids` passes `defect` with context\n   `:parked`; the **same valid record under a key absent from\n   `:ffi-call-ids`** is `:parked-site` (P4); the record with `site` moved\n   to a non-tail call is `:site` (T1 runs before P4).\n7. `refusals`: every refusal row of §5.2 refuses with the named status\n   and kind before any attachment; `first-defect-order`: a body with a\n   noncanonical cursor-cell numbering **and** a tampered window reports\n   `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`.\n8. `a-response-cursor-shared-by-two-waiters-crosses-as-one-cursor-cell` and\n   `a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-not-quiescent`, ported.\n9. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts.\n\n### 8.3 Slice 6c: the layouts, the stack seam, the cross-engine lanes\n\n**6c-pre, the stack tail-completion seam.** File to change:\n`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc` (§4.3): park-entry builders mark a\ntail-call park `:resume-mode :return-result`; `stack-restore` delivers\nsuch an entry by the return transition. Test to create:\n`test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_tail_completion_test.cljc`: a tail\neffectful call parked and resumed delivers through `K` (pops the frame,\ntruncates to its base, pushes the value) and halts with the value when\n`K` is empty; a tail call in operand position never executes the layout\nsyntax after it; non-tail parks are unchanged (the old stack tests stay\ngreen). **Depends on** nothing of 4b or 5.\n\n**6c proper.** Files to create: `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc`\n(§4); `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc`; the two extra\nlanes added to the 6b harness file. **Depends on:** 5a, 5b (`derive`),\n6b, 6c-pre.\n\n**Acceptance (6c).**\n\n1. `layout-test/register-pairing`: for every `P ∈ C`, `phys` is total on\n   every body's named virtuals; `virt(p, s)` is single-valued at every\n   reachable boundary pc (§5.6 item 3).\n2. `layout-test/register-live-is-live-out`: §5.6 item 3's second clause,\n   tail boundaries `[]`.\n3. `layout-test/register-rd-from-a`: on `:worked-example`'s register\n   lane at the inner call's park, the canonical `rd` is `2` while the\n   kernel's `dest` is `3`; the K frame of a nested non-tail call in\n   `:depth-3` has its `rd` from A, not its physical `dest`.\n4. `layout-test/stack-correspondence`: §5.6 item 4.\n5. `layout-test/stack-layout-is-the-saved-set`: §5.6 item 5 and the\n   worked cases: `(f (g x) y)` at the inner call → `[1]`; `(f (if c (g)\n   2) y)` at `(g)` → `[1]`.\n6. `layout-test/stack-slices-partition`: §5.6 item 9; and the\n   multi-frame fixture, the expression `(cat [1] ((fn [x] (cat [2] ((fn\n   [y] (cat [3] (next-of c))) 2))) 1))` under the harness's standard\n   binding setup: `with-cat` outermost, then `(let1 s (stream/make 4)\n   (let1 c (cursor-of s) …))` around it (the stream is made inside the\n   program, as every row does: that is this fixture's chosen setup. A\n   primitive `cat` supplied in the free environment would sit in a live\n   slot and is no carrier value, `:continuation-registers`,\n   `debruijn_register_effects.cljc:196`; an authentic cursor reference is\n   machine data with an explicit carrier marker, `engine.cljc:899-905`, so\n   in-program construction of `c` is a fixture choice, not a carrier\n   restriction). **Derivation of the expression\n   alone** (`cat` and `c` taken as given): the outer application of\n   `(fn [x] …)` pops its closure and `1`, leaving the outer `cat` and\n   `[1]` pushed, so its frame's base is `2`; the inner application leaves\n   the middle `cat` and `[2]` as well, base `4`; the current activation\n   has pushed its `cat` and `[3]` and the read has popped its cursor\n   operand (`stack.cljc:839`), so the operand stack has six values:\n   slices `[0,2)` = `[cat [1]]`, `[2,4)` = `[cat [2]]`, current `[4,6)` =\n   `[cat [3]]`, each slice's `stack-layout` being `[operator-rd\n   literal-rd]` of its `cat` call and equal to that activation's saved\n   window. **As run**, the three binding applications each pop their\n   closure and single operand off an otherwise empty stack, so `K` has\n   **five** frames with bases `0, 0, 0, 2, 4`, slices `[0,0) [0,0) [0,0)\n   [0,2) [2,4)`, current `[4,6)`, stack length six; the test pins these\n   bases from the kernel's state, checks the partition, and checks that\n   lowering the lifted frame emits the same five bases (§4.3; the\n   before-slice rule would emit `0, 0, 0, 0, 2`).\n7. `layout-test/env-reconstruction`: §5.6 item 6.\n8. `layout-test/closures-round-trip`: §5.6 item 7.\n9. `layout-test/tail-lowering-is-unobservable`: §5.6 item 8.\n10. `harness/cross-engine-canonical-equality`: law 4 for every row ×\n    segment under `canonical-under`.\n11. `harness/cross-engine-lowering`: law 5, six ordered pairs.\n12. `harness/layout-refusals`: `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` from a kernel\n    stepped to a non-safepoint pc; a register entry whose `live` was\n    tampered reconstructs a frame the validator refuses (`:window-extra`\n    or `:window-missing` by the tamper's direction).\n13. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts.\n\n### 8.4 Phase 7's entry conditions\n\n**DECIDED** (frozen §10 phase 7). 6a-6c green on three hosts; the row\ncarrier the only writer and reader the semantic-register kernel has; a\ndocumented seam for the holder, checkpoint, ledger and authority paths\n(phase 7 wires it; phase 6 edits none of them); the Stage D/E scenarios\n(`stage_e_scenarios.cljc`, `checkpoint_fixtures.cljc`) listed with, for\neach, the §5.2 row that exercises its parking shape; the export-recovery\nobject (UCF §7.7.4, format version 1 over the old codec) re-based on the\nrow carrier by phase 7, since it embeds a body; and the free-environment\nretention seam (§6.3) either landed by the 4b track or the explicit\n`:free-env` argument threaded through the holder's export path.\n\n### 8.5 Ordering and concurrency\n\n| | needs | concurrent with |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6a | 4b stage 1 (branch) | 4b stage 2, 5a-5c, 6c-pre |\n| 6c-pre | nothing of 4b or 5 | everything |\n| 6b | 4b stage 2; 5c (scanners) | 5a, 5b, 6c-pre |\n| 6c | 5a, 5b, 6b, 6c-pre | 5c |\n\nNo file of 4b or phase 5 is edited. The old kernel file\n`debruijn/stack.cljc` is edited by 6c-pre only, for the seam; the\nregister kernel is not edited. `handoff.cljc` and the old harness are\nnot edited.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Verification honesty\n\n- **Hand-derived numbers.** `saved(4, 2) = {1}` and `L(5)` on the worked\n  example are the phase-3 tests' (`analysis_test.cljc:131-139`). The\n  stack slices `[f]` at the inner call of `(f (g x) y)` and at `(g)` in\n  `(f (if c (g) 2) y)` were derived twice from the §4.3 walk and agreed\n  with the reviewer's derivation; the register `phys(1) = 0`, `phys(2) =\n  3` follow from phase-5 §6.3 row 2, whose pinned `live` at pc 3 is `[0]`\n  (`{T0,T3}` minus the destination `T3`), the same set §4.2 step 4 and\n  §5.6 item 3 compute by subtracting the virtual `rd 2` before mapping.\n  The multi-frame bases in 6c item 6 (`2, 4` for the expression alone;\n  `0, 0, 0, 2, 4` as run under the harness's bindings) were derived\n  twice from the kernel's call arm (`stack.cljc:716-733`, base = height\n  after popping callee and operands); the first pass forgot the pushed\n  operator, and revision 2's lowering rule used the height **before**\n  each slice, which the round-2 review caught and §4.3 now states as\n  cumulative through the slice. Nothing was run.\n- **Claims that are checks, not theorems**: the stack operand slice\n  equals the saved set at non-tail safepoints (§5.6 item 5); the non-push\n  H ↔ A correspondence (item 4); `virt` single-valued at reachable\n  boundaries (item 3); layout `E` = evaluator `E` (item 6); the tail\n  lowering's unused fields are unobservable (item 8); the slices\n  partition the stack (item 9).\n- **What is not claimed**: that kernel state round-trips (shadowed outer\n  positional values are nil-filled; the law is on canonical frames);\n  that every kernel reconstructs canonical frames (two are named; the\n  walker is excluded); that today's stack kernel delivers a tail effect\n  through `K` (it does not; 6c-pre adds it).\n- **Private access.** Every function a test names is public; no `#'`.\n- **Unverified.** 4b stage 2 is not landed: rows 3-4, 7-12, 17, 24 are\n  written against the evaluator design's §1.4-1.6 shapes and the stage-1\n  branch and must be re-read when stage 2 lands. The seam of §4.3 is a\n  specification of a change to `stack.cljc`, not a reading of code that\n  exists.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Findings and proposed amendments\n\nReviewer rulings (codex gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-10-10): F1, F4, U2, U4, U5,\nR1, R2, R7, C1 **ACCEPT**; F2, F3, U1, U3, U6, R3, R4, R5, R6, R8, R9\n**ACCEPT WITH CHANGES**, applied below; dropping `:yin.k/engine`\n**ACCEPTED**; the merged-`E` free environment **REJECTED**, replaced by\n§4.4/§6.3.\n\n### 10.1 To the frozen design (`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`)\n\n**F1 — §4.2 row names (ACCEPT).** Replace \"`:regs` becomes `[segment-A\npc env-cref window-cref k-cref deliver-D]` for an `act` and a sibling\n`:tail-state [segment-A site k-cref deliver-D]` is added\" with: \"the\nframe rows are `:act [segment-A pc env-cref window-cref k-cref rd]` and\n`:tail [segment-A site k-cref]`, the kind being the delivery\ndiscriminant, so `deliver` is not a slot; `:window` is a keyed row\n`[r₁ V₁ r₂ V₂ …]` sorted by `r` in which a nil-valued register is a\npresent `[:lit nil]`; `:kframe` is `[segment-A pc env-cref window-cref\nrd]`; `:stack` and `stack-base` are removed; the root gains `free-env`,\nthe task's initial free environment (continuation design §2, §6.3).\"\n\n**F2 — §4.2 the validator (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** After \"and pending\ncompatibility with `reason`\" insert: \"The validator is the pure function\n`(defect frame code context task)` of `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md`\n§3: `task` is decoded task context (the parked key, the live FFI call\nids, the free environment), never an engine; its rules are ordered,\nstructural checks first, current-window rules on `act` only, return\nwindows separately, and every `E` is checked to agree with the task's\nfree environment off the lexical names; it runs after canonical\nnumbering, as the carrier orders it.\"\n\n**F3 — §4.3 foreign engines (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** After\n\"`lift(lower(frame)) = frame` holds for admitted canonical frames, as\ntoday.\" insert: \"The register kernel pairs physical and virtual\nregisters pc by pc from `v` and `R(v)`, recovers every destination from\nA's call (its `dest` is physical), and resolves each return frame's\nimage and relative pc independently; the stack kernel corresponds the\nnon-push instructions of `H(v)` with `v`, slices its operand stack\n`[previous-base, base_i)` per return frame and `[last-base, count)` for\nthe current activation, and needs a tail-completion seam to deliver a\ntail state through `K` (continuation design §4.3, slice 6c-pre); both\nkernels' positional frames become `E` through the owner chain and\n`bind-params`, with the task's free environment carried explicitly. The\nAST walker is not a frame reconstructor.\"\n\n**F4 — §10 phase 6 (ACCEPT).** Replace \"the row carrier amended\" with\n\"the row carrier amended to body version 3 with one profile,\n`{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`, carrying canonical vectors\nby A, `:yin.k/trees` and the task's free environment, never a native\nimage (continuation design §2, §6)\"; after \"through their layouts\"\ninsert \"(the register and stack kernels, the latter with its\ntail-completion seam; the walker is excluded)\".\n\n### 10.2 To UCF (`yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md`)\n\n**U1 — §7.3.4 `:505-527` (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace `:511`\n\"`:yin.k/carried` carries vectors, not batches.\" with \"`:yin.k/carried`\nand the body's code map carry **register-shaped canonical vectors keyed\nby A**, never batches, never datoms projected from a vector, and never a\nnative stack or register image: a receiver of either native kernel\nderives its image from A (derivations design §2-3). `:yin.k/requires\n:yin.k/trees` maps every address in `:yin.k/segments` to the non-empty\nset of tree addresses the emitter's `source-index` held for it\n(derivations design §9.2).\" **Replace `:513-527`** (\"Loading a fetched\nvector has two paths … nothing may depend on which path a conforming\nengine takes.\") with: \"Loading a fetched vector has **one path**: the\ndirect decode of the canonical vector into an image through the one\nvalidator (`yin.vm.semantic-register.code/well-formed?`). The projection\npath (vector → datoms → loader) is retired (owner ruling 2026-09-18;\n`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §3.4). The conformance obligation is\nthat the two AST projection lanes and the direct vector load yield one\nimage and address (`load_paths_test.cljc`).\"\n\n**U2 — §7.4.1 (ACCEPT).** At its head: \"Superseded for the\nregister-shaped machine by `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §4.1 (two\nstate columns, `act` and `tail`, and the `deliver` record); the table\nbelow describes the stack-shaped machine, which leaves at that design's\nphase 8.\" Replace the `:yin.k/frame` example with §1.2's keyed form.\n\n**U3 — §7.4.2 (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace, in the opening\nparagraph, \"absolute stack depth and environment key sets at a pc depend\non the *activation* — a closure enters with the caller's residual\noperand stack and an environment formed from its captured environment\nplus arguments (`apply-call`), and §2.6 enforces no equal stack heights\nat joins, so the same pc is legitimately reached at many depths\" with\n\"the saved window's values, the environment's bindings and the depth of\n`K` at a pc depend on the *activation*; the same pc is legitimately\nreached under many windows and environments\". Replace \"E, St, and every\nK frame's `:stack-base` and env travel in the value\" with \"E, the saved\nwindow, and every K frame's window, `rd` and env travel in the value, as\ndoes the task's free environment\". In the static map replace\n`[sp :yin.safepoint/stack-effect -1]` with `[sp :yin.safepoint/def #{…}]\n[sp :yin.safepoint/use #{…}] [sp :yin.safepoint/live #{…}]`; in the\nrules replace \"`stack-effect` and `lexically-required` are derived from\nthe canonical vector alone, by the same static walk the linearizer\nperforms (§5.3). They are identical for every engine and checkable\nagainst the reference machine by a conformance test that runs the\nsegment to each safepoint and compares the observed deltas and E-reads.\nAbsolute depth, activation bases, captured environments, and physical\nlayouts are not claimed\" with \"`def`, `use`, `live` and\n`lexically-required` are derived from the canonical vector alone\n(`yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis`). They are identical for every\nengine and checkable against the reference machine by a conformance test\nthat runs the segment to each safepoint and compares the saved window's\nkey set with `live − {rd}` and the E-reads. Window values, environments,\n`K` and physical layouts are not claimed\"; replace \"physical slot →\ncanonical slot\" with \"physical location → virtual register\n(continuation design §4)\".\n\n**U4 — §7.4.3 (ACCEPT).** After \"Three rules make these resumable\":\n\"A pending rides on an `act` state (write-result delivery) or a `tail`\nstate (through-return delivery); the variants are unchanged, and\n`:yin.k/registers R` of the version-2 amendment is the `act`/`tail`\nstate of the frozen design §4.2.\"\n\n**U5 — §7.6 (ACCEPT).** In §7.6.1's example add\n`:yin.k/trees {A #{tree-address …}}  ; §7.6.1a` and a new §7.6.1a with\nthe phase-5 §9.2 UCF row text verbatim, including its completeness\nclause (absent or empty is incomplete).\n\n**U6 — §7.11 (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** In \"Safepoint conformance\nharness\" replace \"including `lift ∘ lower = id`, the static\n`stack-effect`/`lexically-required` checks\" with \"including `lift ∘\nlower = id` on canonical frames, the static `def`/`use`/`live` and\n`lexically-required` checks, the frame validator on every frame, and\n**cross-engine canonical equality**: one program at one safepoint lifts\nto row sets with equal root ids after the harness's specified\nre-emission (continuation design §5.5) from the semantic-register kernel\nand from the stack and register kernels through their layouts, the stack\nkernel with its tail-completion seam\". In §7.11.1 \"Safepoint\nreconstruction\", replace \"Separately prepare two independently\nimplemented UCF engines\" with \"Separately prepare the three engines\nintended to reconstruct canonical frames (the semantic-register kernel;\nthe register kernel; the stack kernel after its tail-completion seam)\"\nand \"the frame, pending wait, next result, and effect trace must agree\nin both directions\" with \"the canonical row set after re-emission, the\npending wait, next result and effect trace must agree across all three\nand in every lowering direction\".\n\n### 10.3 To the row-carrier draft (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`)\n\nThe inventory below is every clause the grep of the draft for\n\"legacy\", \"version 0/1/2\", \"semantic profile only / semantic-only\",\n\"does not translate\", \"unchanged / do not move\", \"other profile\",\n\"registry\" found operative; each is replaced or deleted.\n\n**R1 — §2 `:50-81` (ACCEPT).** Replace the section with: \"**Body\nversion 3, one profile.** The carrier is body version 3 and reads no\nother version (owner, 2026-10-11: no legacy): a body of version 0, 1 or\n2 is `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` at the gate and is never normalised or\nupgraded. The profile map is `{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`;\nthere is no engine key, because the frame is the canonical\nregister-shaped machine's and the executing kernel is the receiving\ncomposition's choice: the stack and register kernels lower the same rows\nthrough their layouts (`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md`\n§2.1, §4). Any other profile map is `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`.\"\n\n**R1a — status paragraph `:18-20`.** Replace \"Body versions 0, 1 and 2\nkeep their grammar, readers and bytes; this document proposes a fourth\nbody version whose carrier is rows\" with \"This document specifies body\nversion 3, the one carrier; older bodies are not read.\"\n\n**R2 — §5.2 `:298-317` (ACCEPT).** Replace with continuation §2.3's\ntable and notes.\n\n**R3 — §5.1 `:287-296` (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace the `:reified`\nrow with `| :reified | act-cref | a captured continuation: the decoded\nact state of frozen §4.2, no pending |`; replace \"`{:yin.k/tag\n:yin.k/frame :yin.k/registers R}`\" and \"`{:yin.k/tag :yin.k/frame\n:yin.k/parked-id P}`: resolves in the task's parked table; never\nduplicates `R`\" with the keyed `act` state and \"resolves in the task's\nparked table; never duplicates the state\"; replace \"A reified value's\nregisters are validated in captured-value context (amendment §7): its pc\nmust be a `:current-continuation` site's successor, not a wait or park\nsafepoint\" with \"A reified value's act is validated in context\n`:captured` (continuation §3.2 P3): its `pc−1` is a `:current-continuation`\nand it has no pending\"; and replace \"a reified value becomes a\nreceiver-owned native continuation from `R`\" with \"from its act\".\n\n**R4 — §5.4 `:361` (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace `:parked-table |\nP₁ regs-cref₁ P₂ regs-cref₂ …` with `P₁ state-cref₁ …` (an `:act` or a\n`:tail`), and add: \"Validation of a parked state reads decoded task\ncontext, never an engine: the table key `P` and the set of call ids the\ntask's live `:ffi`/`:ffi-request` pendings carry are the `task` input of\n`frame/defect` (continuation §3.1), under which an `:act` at a `:park`\nsite is an explicit park and an `:act` at an `:ffi-call` site or a\n`:tail` at a tail call under a live call id is FFI bookkeeping.\"\n\n**R5 — §5.5 `:383-401` (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace the root with\ncontinuation §2.6 (adds `free-env-cref`; `contract` is the one profile\nmap; `code` is `{A \"v4\"-vector}`; `requires` gains `:yin.k/trees`); in\n`:394` replace \"`requires ; plain: UCF §7.6.1's map, unchanged`\" with\n\"`requires ; plain: UCF §7.6.1's map plus :yin.k/trees`\".\n\n**R6 — §8 step 7 `:661-667` (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace with:\n\"**Frames.** Every `:act`, `:tail`, `:kframe`, `:reified` and\nparked-table state is decoded to its keyed frame and judged by\n`yin.vm.semantic-register.frame/defect` with its context (`:wait`,\n`:captured`, `:parked`) and the decoded task context (parked key, live\nFFI call ids, the root's free environment); a defect is\n`:yin.k/undecodable` with the rule's kind and the row path (continuation\n§3). This step runs after canonical numbering (step 6) and before\npending validation (step 8).\"\n\n**R6a — §8 step 1 `:618-623`.** Replace \"then every profile map against\nthe registry (only the semantic profile is supported, §2)\" with \"then\nevery profile map against the one profile map of §2\".\n\n**R7 — `:63-68` and §10.4 `:774-777` (ACCEPT).** Delete \"Code stamps\n`\"v3\"`, `\"b2\"`, `\"r2\"` and the inner version 1 do not move: this is a\nchange of carrier, not of instruction, scheduler, or value semantics,\nexactly the distinction the amendment draws between its versions and\nexecutable code.\" Replace §10.4 with: \"**Contract stamp.** The code\ncontract carried is `\"v4\"`, the register-shaped machine's; the carrier\nversion is 3; the two are independent, and neither names a legacy\nvalue.\"\n\n**R8 — §9 `:737-746` \"Legacy correspondence\" and §10.8 `:797-801`\n(ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Delete both: there is no legacy reader and no\nnormalisation tool. In §10.3 `:769-773` delete \"Versions 0, 1 and 2\nremain compatibility inputs. One canonical nested projection of version\n3 is kept for single-message channels and must stay exactly mutually\ninverse with the rows.\" and \"Retiring old readers is an owner\nversion-support decision\", leaving \"Rows are the carrier authority.\"\nIn §9's law list delete \"Exact mutual inversion is required only between\nversion 3 and its one canonical nested projection (§10.3)\".\n\n**R9 — §10.6 `:782-788`, §10.7 `:792-796`, §2 `:70-81`, §10's\nproposals list `:821-834`, \"Still open\" `:836-837`, §11 `:839-852`\n(ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** §10.6, **whole item**: replace its opening\n\"**Foreign-engine value profiles.** Required before any implementation\nbrief claims heterogeneous execution conformance, and not drafted here\"\nwith \"**Foreign-engine value profiles.** Required before an\nimplementation brief claims execution conformance for an engine\n**outside the three repository lanes** (the semantic-register kernel and\nthe stack and register kernels, whose reconstruction is the layouts of\n`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §4 and needs no value\nprofile), and not drafted here\"; keep its list of what such a profile\nmust cover; and replace \"version 3, like version 2, does\nnot translate between kernels\" with \"version 3 carries the canonical\nframe; a stack or register kernel reconstructs it through its layout\n(continuation §4), which is heterogeneous reconstruction, not\ntranslation between native formats; foreign-engine *value* profiles for\nengines outside this repository remain a separate document\". §10.7:\ndelete (\"there are no other profile tables\"). Proposals list: delete\n\"semantic-only initial scope\"; add \"one engine-less profile (continuation\n§2.1)\" and \"the explicit root `free-env` (§6.3)\". \"Still open\": replace\nwith \"none beyond the work-bound limits (§10.10)\". §11: replace \"Code\nidentity, the contract stamp and profile registry, safepoints,\" with\n\"Code identity (A), safepoints,\"; delete \"versions 0-2\" references.\n\n**R10 — §5.5 `:421-426` custody paragraph.** Replace \"a version-3 fork\nroot is admitted exactly as a version-0 body is, proposes nothing, and\nis never upgraded to custody\" with \"a fork root proposes nothing and is\nnever upgraded to custody; an exclusive-only receiver refuses it as\n`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`\".\n\n**R11 — §3 `:115-134`.** Keep verbatim, including \"**body version 3\nuses BLAKE3 permanently**\" and the per-id algorithm check (the reviewer\nasked that this explicit rule survive).\n\n**U7 — scope and precedence of UCF's historical legacy-body clauses\n(new).** UCF keeps clauses that describe bodies the row carrier never\nreads: §7.2.1 (versions 0 and 1, `:166-321`), the version-0/1 custody\ngate and fork rules (`:234-290`), §7.4.3 r5's version-0 notes (`:966-970`:\n\"A version-0 entry without a phase reads as `:running`\", \"The landed\nversion-0 reader breaches both\"), §7.7.4's `nil`-header version-0 lift\nand recovery of legacy fork bytes (`:1781`, `:1806-1807`, `:1844`), and\n§7.11.1's version-0/1 interoperation rows (`:3051-3057`, `:3095-3096`).\nInsert at the head of §7.2.1: \"**Scope (2026-10-11).** Body versions 0,\n1 and 2 and every clause of this document that admits, reads, recovers\nor interoperates with them are **historical**: they describe the\nstack-shaped machine's handoff, which leaves at\n`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §10 phase 8. The row carrier of body\nversion 3 (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md` as amended by\n`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md`) reads no other version and\ntakes **precedence** over any sentence below that implies otherwise; a\nconflict is resolved in its favour without further amendment. **Not\nhistorical**: the custody, fencing and operation-id semantics (§7.7.8,\n§7.9, §7.4.3's operation ids) travel in version 3 as the root's\n`custody` slot (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md` §5.5) and stay\noperative; where those sections say 'a version-1 body' read, for version\n3, 'a root whose custody policy is `:yin.k/exclusive`', and where they\nsay 'a version-0 body' or 'fork', 'a root whose policy is `:yin.k/fork`'\n(§5.5's table). The code stamp `{:yin.code/contract \"v3\" :yin.k/version\n0}` wherever this document shows it (§7.2's example `:121`, §7.2.1\n`:183`, §7.3.3 `:232-236`) is the stack-shaped machine's; the\nregister-shaped machine's contract is `\"v4\"`\n(`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §6), the one the version-3 profile map\nnames, and §7.2's envelope example is superseded for version 3 by the\nrow carrier's wire unit (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md` §3, ids under\nJing's default digest).\" The same grep (`legacy`, `version-0`,\n`version 0`, `versions 0`, `version 1`, `recovery`) found, besides the\nclauses above: the export-recovery object's version-1 format\n(`:1789-1807`), which is phase 7's to re-base on the row carrier and is\nnamed in §8.4 as an entry condition, not amended here; publication\nfailure recovery (`:1741`), completion recovery (`:2417`) and the\nledger's \"legacy destructive readers\" (`:2774-2775`), which concern the\ndriver, the ledger protocol and the ledger reader, not a body version,\nand are untouched; and the status paragraph `:39-42`, covered by the\nscope statement's \"every clause\".\n\n### 10.4 To code-as-tuples (`yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`) §7.2\n\n**C1 (ACCEPT).** Replace the first paragraph with: \"The vector-to-datoms\nprojection path is **retired** (owner ruling 2026-09-18; frozen §3.4\n'One vector validator'). There is one load path for a vector, the direct\none, and two AST projection lanes (datom lane, row lane) that produce\nthe vector; all three feed one validator\n(`yin.vm.semantic-register.code/well-formed?`). UCF §7.3.4's projection\npath is superseded accordingly.\" Replace obligation 2's second sentence\nwith \"loading the vector produced by either AST lane and the vector\nloaded directly yield the same image and address (`load_paths_test.cljc`)\",\nand obligation 3's \"both paths refuse with the same defect\" with \"the\ndirect vector load refuses with the published defect (rule and pc) for\nevery rule of the frozen §3.4\". Obligations 1 and 4 stand.\n\n### 10.5 Checked and consistent (no amendment)\n\nFrozen §2.4 delivery shapes against the 4b branch; frozen §4.1 two state\ncolumns; the evaluator design §1.3-1.6; the draft's §3, §4, §5.1 (except\n`:reified`), §5.3, §6, §7 and §8 steps 1-6, 8-12; v2 amendment §2's `E`\nshape; the phase-5 §9.2 `:yin.k/trees` text; the register kernel's\n`:return-result` delivery (`register.cljc:458-468`).\n\n---\n\n## 11. Owner questions\n\n**None.** The reviewer accepted the engine-less profile and rejected the\nmerged-`E` free environment; both are now settled in the text. Nothing\nremaining is owner-level.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Portability notes for the implementer\n\n1. **Nil-valued window keys (Dart, Node).** The window is built with\n   `select-keys` and encoded as `[r [:lit nil]]`; never filter `some?`\n   values; `frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member` over row 22\n   (`(pair nil (next-of c))`, the nil operand evaluated before the read)\n   is the canary. Membership is always by `contains?`/key sets, never\n   `(get W r)`.\n2. **`for` over large seqs (Dart).** Row sets of the C4 modules run to\n   thousands of rows; build with `mapv`/`into`/`reduce`.\n3. **Reader whitespace before closers (Dart).** Pinned row sets are\n   Clojure data in `.cljc`, never EDN strings.\n4. **Duplicate protocol params (Dart).** `gc-children [_ _x]`\n   (`srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:386`); any new protocol method\n   in `layout` likewise.\n5. **Multi-key `assoc` on nil (Dart).** Frames and windows start from\n   `{}` (`handoff.cljc:1455-1457` records the trap).\n6. **Reader conditionals.** `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)`\n   with `:cljd` first; `:clj`-only source-reading tests as `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)`.\n7. **Private var access (Dart).** Every function named in §8 is public;\n   no `#'`.\n8. **Sorted keys.** Window and bindings rows are sorted by Jing\n   canonical bytes of the key, never by host `sort` on mixed types.\n9. **Numeric classes (Node).** `pc`, `rd`, `r`, `site` are exact\n   integers; compare with `cbor/numeric-kind` before `=` on wire values\n   (`ucf/profile-engine`, `ucf.cljc:77-91`, is the template).\n10. **Fresh worktree.** `mise trust` and `npm ci` before the Node lane.\n","numLines":915,"startLine":848,"totalLines":1762}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01W7MZUGNUwBZNBjWQ2godft","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
