{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AzEqnDSErZdcRPjzMrMV9t","type":"tool_result","content":"376\t`frame/defect` (continuation §3.1), under which an `:act` at a `:park`\n377\tsite is an explicit park and an `:act` at an `:ffi-call` site or a\n378\t`:tail` at a tail call under a live call id is FFI bookkeeping.\n379\t\n380\tResource entries never appear in `:store`; streams and cursor cells lower into\n381\tthe receiver's private resource table beside the program store (linker\n382\tM4, `yin.vm.linker.md` 7.3). `:module-store` rows are the per-module\n383\tsnapshots of §7.6.2's M4 paragraph. The parked table holds exactly the\n384\treachable records. An `:install` row carries the complete entry of\n385\t§7.4.3 r5: phase `:running` or `:parked`, parent link id (nil where the\n386\tcontract permits), the response verbatim as structural data, and the\n387\tchild as a cref to a whole `:task` row in the child role. \"Verified\"\n388\tmeans verified by the **receiver**, never trusted because it decodes:\n389\tthe response's manifest names the module the row is keyed by, its link\n390\tid equals `parent`, its image is well formed, hashes to the address it\n391\tis delivered under, is the image the manifest names, and its format,\n392\tcontract and the child's profile agree (`yin.vm.linker.md` §5, §9;\n393\tamendment §2). A failure is `:yin.k/undecodable` naming the row.\n394\t\n395\t### 5.5 The root\n396\t\n397\t```clojure\n398\t[T :task\n399\t   version          ; 3                       (gated first, §8)\n400\t   contract         ; {:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}, the one profile map (§2)\n401\t   kind             ; :blocked | :parked | :halted\n402\t   role             ; :root | :child\n403\t   id-counter       ; N                       (UCF §7.6.3)\n404\t   free-env-cref    ; a :bindings row, the task's initial free environment (continuation §6.3)\n405\t   store-cref\n406\t   module-stores    ; crefs sorted by M\n407\t   parked-cref      ; :parked-table\n408\t   cursor-cells-cref       ; :cursor-cells census\n409\t   requires         ; plain: UCF §7.6.1's map plus :yin.k/trees (continuation §6.1)\n410\t   code             ; plain: {A canonical-vector …}, \"v4\" vectors verified to hash to their key\n411\t   installs         ; crefs to :install rows, sorted by module name\n412\t   frames           ; crefs to :wait rows, IN WAIT ORDER   (:blocked, :parked)\n413\t   parked-id        ; P or nil                              (:parked only)\n414\t   result           ; V or nil                              (:halted only)\n415\t   custody]         ; plain, see below\n416\t```\n417\t\n418\t(Root replaced 2026-10-11 by continuation §2.6: `free-env-cref` added,\n419\t`contract` is the one profile map, `code` holds `\"v4\"` canonical vectors,\n420\t`requires` gains `:yin.k/trees`.) No `layout` slot and no native image:\n421\tthose were the positional profiles' (v2 amendment §2, §4.1).\n422\t\n423\tKind rules are §7.2.1's: `:blocked` has nonempty frames and neither\n424\tparked-id nor result; `:parked` has frames (possibly empty), a parked-id\n425\tnaming a key of the parked table, no result; `:halted` has a result and\n426\tneither frames nor parked-id. Frames restore in carried order and are\n427\tnever collapsed to one; a task with an empty ready queue may hold several\n428\tordered waits.\n429\t\n430\t`custody` is the custody arm carried as plain data, under the rules of\n431\t§7.2.1 and amendment §3, by role, kind and policy:\n432\t\n433\t| role | kind | policy | `custody` |\n434\t|---|---|---|---|\n435\t| root | blocked / parked | exclusive | `{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq}` plus `:yin.k/origin` on every successor, absent on a first export |\n436\t| root | blocked / parked | fork | `{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/fork}` |\n437\t| root | halted | exclusive | `{:yin.k/origin …}` only: a result is not a lease subject |\n438\t| root | halted | fork | nil: a fork halt has no custody data and a first fork halt has no origin to carry |\n439\t| child | any | — | nil; validated with its root's occurrence, origin and counter passed down |\n440\t\n441\tThe explicit fork policy spelling projects onto the amendment's\n442\tempty-header fork representation: a fork root proposes nothing and is\n443\tnever upgraded to custody; an exclusive-only receiver refuses it as\n444\t`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`. Admission semantics are the governing ones\n445\tunchanged; only the spelling is new. No body carries an epoch."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02df6bdc-04b9-48af-9b17-9798293c08e5","uuid":"562388af-f422-4a14-a526-4d222088ec70","timestamp":"2026-10-12T17:42:20.169Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-6b-amend/docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md","content":"`frame/defect` (continuation §3.1), under which an `:act` at a `:park`\nsite is an explicit park and an `:act` at an `:ffi-call` site or a\n`:tail` at a tail call under a live call id is FFI bookkeeping.\n\nResource entries never appear in `:store`; streams and cursor cells lower into\nthe receiver's private resource table beside the program store (linker\nM4, `yin.vm.linker.md` 7.3). `:module-store` rows are the per-module\nsnapshots of §7.6.2's M4 paragraph. The parked table holds exactly the\nreachable records. An `:install` row carries the complete entry of\n§7.4.3 r5: phase `:running` or `:parked`, parent link id (nil where the\ncontract permits), the response verbatim as structural data, and the\nchild as a cref to a whole `:task` row in the child role. \"Verified\"\nmeans verified by the **receiver**, never trusted because it decodes:\nthe response's manifest names the module the row is keyed by, its link\nid equals `parent`, its image is well formed, hashes to the address it\nis delivered under, is the image the manifest names, and its format,\ncontract and the child's profile agree (`yin.vm.linker.md` §5, §9;\namendment §2). A failure is `:yin.k/undecodable` naming the row.\n\n### 5.5 The root\n\n```clojure\n[T :task\n   version          ; 3                       (gated first, §8)\n   contract         ; {:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}, the one profile map (§2)\n   kind             ; :blocked | :parked | :halted\n   role             ; :root | :child\n   id-counter       ; N                       (UCF §7.6.3)\n   free-env-cref    ; a :bindings row, the task's initial free environment (continuation §6.3)\n   store-cref\n   module-stores    ; crefs sorted by M\n   parked-cref      ; :parked-table\n   cursor-cells-cref       ; :cursor-cells census\n   requires         ; plain: UCF §7.6.1's map plus :yin.k/trees (continuation §6.1)\n   code             ; plain: {A canonical-vector …}, \"v4\" vectors verified to hash to their key\n   installs         ; crefs to :install rows, sorted by module name\n   frames           ; crefs to :wait rows, IN WAIT ORDER   (:blocked, :parked)\n   parked-id        ; P or nil                              (:parked only)\n   result           ; V or nil                              (:halted only)\n   custody]         ; plain, see below\n```\n\n(Root replaced 2026-10-11 by continuation §2.6: `free-env-cref` added,\n`contract` is the one profile map, `code` holds `\"v4\"` canonical vectors,\n`requires` gains `:yin.k/trees`.) No `layout` slot and no native image:\nthose were the positional profiles' (v2 amendment §2, §4.1).\n\nKind rules are §7.2.1's: `:blocked` has nonempty frames and neither\nparked-id nor result; `:parked` has frames (possibly empty), a parked-id\nnaming a key of the parked table, no result; `:halted` has a result and\nneither frames nor parked-id. Frames restore in carried order and are\nnever collapsed to one; a task with an empty ready queue may hold several\nordered waits.\n\n`custody` is the custody arm carried as plain data, under the rules of\n§7.2.1 and amendment §3, by role, kind and policy:\n\n| role | kind | policy | `custody` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| root | blocked / parked | exclusive | `{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq}` plus `:yin.k/origin` on every successor, absent on a first export |\n| root | blocked / parked | fork | `{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/fork}` |\n| root | halted | exclusive | `{:yin.k/origin …}` only: a result is not a lease subject |\n| root | halted | fork | nil: a fork halt has no custody data and a first fork halt has no origin to carry |\n| child | any | — | nil; validated with its root's occurrence, origin and counter passed down |\n\nThe explicit fork policy spelling projects onto the amendment's\nempty-header fork representation: a fork root proposes nothing and is\nnever upgraded to custody; an exclusive-only receiver refuses it as\n`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`. Admission semantics are the governing ones\nunchanged; only the spelling is new. No body carries an epoch.","numLines":70,"startLine":376,"totalLines":949}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AzEqnDSErZdcRPjzMrMV9t","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
