{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YbQPsffJJivyc1htLGNqhJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1421\t(defn- advance-install\n1422\t  \"Step the install child of `module-name` in this round, beside every\n1423\t   other task (section 7.3): `running` runs it until it halts or parks.\n1424\t   A parked child stays `parked`; a halted one goes on to `validated`; an\n1425\t   error refuses the install. An error while publishing -- attaching an\n1426\t   origin image, lowering the slice or a store snapshot, or receiving a\n1427\t   dependency -- refuses it too, at phase `:linked`, from the state the\n1428\t   round started with: nothing half-published survives, every waiter is\n1429\t   restored with the refusal, and no throw leaves the round.\n1430\t\n1431\t   Under a custody gate the child is stamped with the root's mode before\n1432\t   it runs; in `:exporting` and `:ended` it does not run.\"\n1433\t  [state module-name]\n1434\t  (let [inst (get-in state [:installs module-name])\n1435\t        mode (vm/gate-mode state)\n1436\t        [child refusal]\n1437\t        (when-not (contains? #{:exporting :ended} mode)\n1438\t          (try [(vm/run (stamp-gate (:vm inst) mode)) nil]\n1439\t               (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n1440\t                 [nil (error-refusal module-name e)])))]\n1441\t    (cond\n1442\t      (and (nil? child) (nil? refusal)) state\n1443\t      refusal (refuse-install state module-name refusal)\n1444\t      (:blocked? child)\n1445\t      (assoc-in state [:installs module-name]\n1446\t                (assoc inst :vm child :phase :parked))\n1447\t      (:halted? child)\n1448\t      (try (link-install state module-name (assoc inst :vm child))\n1449\t           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n1450\t             (refuse-install state module-name\n1451\t                             (assoc (error-refusal module-name e)\n1452\t                                    :phase :linked))))\n1453\t      :else (assoc-in state [:installs module-name]\n1454\t                      (assoc inst :vm child :phase :running)))))\n1455\t\n1456\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02df6bdc-04b9-48af-9b17-9798293c08e5","uuid":"8931f10b-d9b3-4a80-ba29-e1c6bb583a55","timestamp":"2026-10-12T17:42:58.071Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-6b-amend/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc","content":"(defn- advance-install\n  \"Step the install child of `module-name` in this round, beside every\n   other task (section 7.3): `running` runs it until it halts or parks.\n   A parked child stays `parked`; a halted one goes on to `validated`; an\n   error refuses the install. An error while publishing -- attaching an\n   origin image, lowering the slice or a store snapshot, or receiving a\n   dependency -- refuses it too, at phase `:linked`, from the state the\n   round started with: nothing half-published survives, every waiter is\n   restored with the refusal, and no throw leaves the round.\n\n   Under a custody gate the child is stamped with the root's mode before\n   it runs; in `:exporting` and `:ended` it does not run.\"\n  [state module-name]\n  (let [inst (get-in state [:installs module-name])\n        mode (vm/gate-mode state)\n        [child refusal]\n        (when-not (contains? #{:exporting :ended} mode)\n          (try [(vm/run (stamp-gate (:vm inst) mode)) nil]\n               (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n                 [nil (error-refusal module-name e)])))]\n    (cond\n      (and (nil? child) (nil? refusal)) state\n      refusal (refuse-install state module-name refusal)\n      (:blocked? child)\n      (assoc-in state [:installs module-name]\n                (assoc inst :vm child :phase :parked))\n      (:halted? child)\n      (try (link-install state module-name (assoc inst :vm child))\n           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n             (refuse-install state module-name\n                             (assoc (error-refusal module-name e)\n                                    :phase :linked))))\n      :else (assoc-in state [:installs module-name]\n                      (assoc inst :vm child :phase :running)))))\n\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1421,"totalLines":2789}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YbQPsffJJivyc1htLGNqhJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
