{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfxksnZfEqtVjyNRtb2Um","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D2NFUHrhD8fTxG7zYFFusN","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-6b-amend/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md","old_string":"- **Install children** are whole `:task` rows in the child role (draft\n  §5.4, §5.5), unchanged.","new_string":"- **Install children** are whole `:task` rows in the child role (draft\n  §5.4, §5.5), unchanged.\n\n**Amended after 6b (2026-10-13), what travels and what does not**\n(engineer deviations 4, 6, 7; codex round 1 accepted all three):\n\n- **The store slice is the whole root store.** `lift-task` walks every\n  entry of `(:store m)` (`store-node`), and every parked record travels\n  (`parked-table` over all of `(:parked m)`), each judged by P4. No\n  reachability pruning of the store is performed. *Why:* the kernel\n  holds no liveness information for store entries; the conservative\n  slice is correct and the draft's \"exactly the reachable records\" was\n  never implemented.\n- **Module stores travel by reachability.** A `:module-store` row is\n  emitted for every `store-of` an `E` or closure names, transitively\n  through the values of stores already discovered (`module-store-nodes`);\n  a named store the kernel lacks is `:yin.k/non-portable\n  :missing-module-store`.\n- **Linked registry entries do not travel.** The row table has no slot\n  for the receiver's module registry; only module stores do. A name a\n  carried closure resolves through the source's registry is a\n  **composition prerequisite** of the receiver: row 17's receiver is\n  given the source's registry value, and without it the relift refuses\n  `:yin.k/unsatisfied {:obligations #{host.mod/f}}`. The receiver's\n  registry is kept as given; there is no isolated-receiver pruning.\n- **Custody is nil at the root in phase 6.** The lift emits `custody nil`\n  (fork), and the lower refuses any non-nil custody as `:yin.k/unsupported\n  :custody`; the exclusive and holder path is phase 7 (§8.4)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1985,"cache_read_input_tokens":154945,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1985},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02df6bdc-04b9-48af-9b17-9798293c08e5","uuid":"7274a342-a4b7-4253-91f5-89b83413c50e","timestamp":"2026-10-12T17:43:39.985Z","request_id":"req_011CfxksnBL4oyKBiMsdwzBe","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01D2NFUHrhD8fTxG7zYFFusN":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-6b-amend/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md","old_string":"- **Install children** are whole `:task` rows in the child role (draft\n  §5.4, §5.5), unchanged.","new_string":"- **Install children** are whole `:task` rows in the child role (draft\n  §5.4, §5.5), unchanged.\n\n**Amended after 6b (2026-10-13), what travels and what does not**\n(engineer deviations 4, 6, 7; codex round 1 accepted all three):\n\n- **The store slice is the whole root store.** `lift-task` walks every\n  entry of `(:store m)` (`store-node`), and every parked record travels\n  (`parked-table` over all of `(:parked m)`), each judged by P4. No\n  reachability pruning of the store is performed. *Why:* the kernel\n  holds no liveness information for store entries; the conservative\n  slice is correct and the draft's \"exactly the reachable records\" was\n  never implemented.\n- **Module stores travel by reachability.** A `:module-store` row is\n  emitted for every `store-of` an `E` or closure names, transitively\n  through the values of stores already discovered (`module-store-nodes`);\n  a named store the kernel lacks is `:yin.k/non-portable\n  :missing-module-store`.\n- **Linked registry entries do not travel.** The row table has no slot\n  for the receiver's module registry; only module stores do. A name a\n  carried closure resolves through the source's registry is a\n  **composition prerequisite** of the receiver: row 17's receiver is\n  given the source's registry value, and without it the relift refuses\n  `:yin.k/unsatisfied {:obligations #{host.mod/f}}`. The receiver's\n  registry is kept as given; there is no isolated-receiver pruning.\n- **Custody is nil at the root in phase 6.** The lift emits `custody nil`\n  (fork), and the lower refuses any non-nil custody as `:yin.k/unsupported\n  :custody`; the exclusive and holder path is phase 7 (§8.4)."}}}
