{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011Cfxku76ARwFMpbEHgTisi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N9KMTPnCU6RHBd2vqUY5ua","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-6b-amend/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md","old_string":"`[:captured :arg r]` (`(cat (cat (cat [] k) y) r)` with `k = :captured`,\n`y = :arg`). **Frames the wrappers add.**","new_string":"`[:captured :arg r]` (`(cat (cat (cat [] k) y) r)` with `k = :captured`,\n`y = :arg`). **Amended after 6b (2026-10-13), one exception to the\nmechanical rule (B2):** `nest`'s own lambda parameter is `x`, so under\n`:depth-3` any row whose program captures the free name `x` captures the\nwrapper's `x` instead. Row 21 is the one such row: its `(fn [] x)` is\ncreated inside the innermost `nest` application where `x = 1`, so the\nreference run itself answers `[3 [2 [1 1]]]`, not `[3 [2 [1 99]]]`, and\nthe harness pins `1` for that one case (`safepoint_harness_test.cljc`,\nthe `(and (= 21 n) (= :depth-3 label))` branch). The bare, `:operand`\nand `:captured` results of row 21 keep `99`. The wrapper rule is\notherwise unchanged; the exception is stated rather than the wrapper\nrenamed, because the old harness's segments are shared and the lowered\nrun matches the reference either way (law 1 holds on the row). **Frames\nthe wrappers add.**"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":524,"cache_read_input_tokens":157882,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":524},"output_tokens":63,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02df6bdc-04b9-48af-9b17-9798293c08e5","uuid":"b538b66a-f032-45e7-8faa-0cee6635b1be",